paid within the prescribed deadline, as applications without successful fee payment are treated as incomplete.</p><h3>Selection Process</h3><p>The selection process for this recruitment consists of a Phase-I preliminary examination, a Phase-II main examination, and an interview.  The final merit list is prepared strictly on the basis of the candidate''''s performance in the prescribed stages, subject to document verification and fulfilment of all eligibility conditions. Candidates are advised to prepare thoroughly for each stage and to keep track of the official announcements regarding the examination schedule and results.</p><h3>How to Apply</h3><p>Eligible and interested candidates must apply online through the official website https://www.nabard.org within the application window. The step-by-step procedure involves registering with a valid email address and mobile number, filling in the personal, educational and communication details, uploading the scanned photograph, signature and required documents in the prescribed format and size, paying the application fee, and finally submitting the completed application form. Candidates are advised to take a printout of the submitted application form and the fee receipt for future reference, and to avoid waiting until the last date to prevent any last-minute technical difficulties.</p>', 'Bank', 'NABARD', 'National Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development', 'notification', '2026-06-05', '2026-06-06', '2026-06-08', '2026-06-28', '2026-06-28', '2026-08-09', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 120, '21 to 30 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories', 'a Bachelor''''s Degree with a minimum of 60% marks (50% for SC/ST/PwBD), or a Post Graduate degree with the prescribed marks, in the relevant discipline such as Agriculture, Economics, Finance, or allied subjects from a recognized University', 'Candidates applying for specialist posts must possess the specific professional or academic qualification 