(NULL, 'LIC AAO 2026 – Assistant Administrative Officer Recruitment', 'lic-aao-2026-assistant-administrative-officer', 'Life Insurance Corporation of India has released the LIC AAO 2026 notification for recruitment of Assistant Administrative Officers in Generalist and specialist disciplines. Graduates can apply online at licindia.in.', '<h2>LIC AAO 2026 – Assistant Administrative Officer Recruitment – Complete Recruitment Overview</h2><p>The Life Insurance Corporation of India has released the official notification for the recruitment to the post of <strong>LIC AAO 2026</strong>. This recruitment is a valuable opportunity for eligible candidates across the country to secure a stable and respectable government career with attractive pay, allowances, job security and excellent avenues for professional growth. Interested candidates who fulfil the prescribed eligibility conditions are advised to read the complete official notification carefully before submitting their online application on the official website https://licindia.in.</p><h3>About the Post & Organisation</h3><p>The Life Insurance Corporation of India conducts this recruitment to fill the post of LIC AAO 2026 through a transparent and merit-based selection process. The AAO post offers an attractive salary, perks and a respected managerial career in the country''''s largest life insurer. The selected candidates will be entitled to the pay scale prescribed under the applicable pay matrix along with dearness allowance, house rent allowance, transport allowance and other admissible benefits as per the rules of the organisation. The post offers a structured career path with opportunities for promotion to higher grades based on seniority and departmental examinations.</p><h3>Important Dates</h3><ul><li>Notification Release: 4 June 2026</li><li>Application Start: 6 June 2026</li><li>Last Date to Apply: 26 June 2026</li><li>Preliminary Examination: August 2026 (Tentative)</li><li>Main Examination: September 2026 (Tentative)</li></ul><h3>Eligibility & Educational Qualification</h3><p>To be eligible for this recruitment, candidates must satisfy the educational qualification requirement, which is as follows: a Bachelor''''s or Master''''s Degree from a recognized Indian University or institution with a minimum of 60% marks for the Generalist post, and the relevant professional qualification for specialist posts such as Chartered Accountant, Actuarial, Legal or IT. Candidates applying for specialist posts must hold the specific qualification prescribed for the respective discipline, and knowledge of the regional language is desirable. Candidates are strongly advised to verify that they meet all the prescribed academic and eligibility conditions as on the cut-off date mentioned in the official notification, since applications that do not meet the requirements are liable to be rejected at any stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>Age Limit & Relaxation</h3><p>The age limit prescribed for this recruitment is 21 to 30 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories. Age relaxation is provided to candidates belonging to reserved categories as per the rules of the Government and the organisation, namely five years for SC and ST candidates, three years for OBC candidates, ten years for Persons with Benchmark Disabilities, and additional relaxation for Ex-Servicemen and other special categories as specified in the detailed notification.</p><h3>Application Fee</h3><p>The prescribed application fee must be paid online through net banking, debit card, credit card, UPI or other digital payment modes available on the portal. Candidates belonging to SC, ST, Persons with Disabilities, Ex-Servicemen and, in many cases, women candidates are eligible for fee exemption or a reduced fee as per the category-wise fee structure mentioned in the notification. Candidates should ensure that the fee is paid within the prescribed deadline, as applications without successful fee payment are treated as incomplete.</p><h3>Selection Process</h3><p>The selection process for this recruitment consists of an online preliminary examination, an online main examination, and an interview followed by a pre-recruitment medical examination.  The final merit list is prepared strictly on the basis of the candidate''''s performance in the prescribed stages, subject to document verification and fulfilment of all eligibility conditions. Candidates are advised to prepare thoroughly for each stage and to keep track of the official announcements regarding the examination schedule and results.</p><h3>How to Apply</h3><p>Eligible and interested candidates must apply online through the official website https://licindia.in within the application window. The step-by-step procedure involves registering with a valid email address and mobile number, filling in the personal, educational and communication details, uploading the scanned photograph, signature and required documents in the prescribed format and size, paying the application fee, and finally submitting the completed application form. Candidates are advised to take a printout of the submitted application form and the fee receipt for future reference, and to avoid waiting until the last date to prevent any last-minute technical difficulties.</p>', 'Insurance', 'LIC', 'Life Insurance Corporation of India', 'notification', '2026-06-04', '2026-06-05', '2026-06-06', '2026-06-26', '2026-06-26', '2026-08-08', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 300, '21 to 30 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories', 'a Bachelor''''s or Master''''s Degree from a recognized Indian University or institution with a minimum of 60% marks for the Generalist post, and the relevant professional qualification for specialist posts such as Chartered Accountant, Actuarial, Legal or IT', 'Candidates applying for specialist posts must hold the specific qualification prescribed for the respective discipline, and knowledge of the regional language is desirable.', 700.00, 700.00, 85.00, 'https://licindia.in', 'https://licindia.in', 'https://licindia.in/notifications/aao-2026.pdf', 'https://licindia.in/careers', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ACTIVE', 1, 1, 'LIC AAO 2026 – Apply Online for Assistant Administrative Officer', 'LIC AAO 2026 recruitment for Assistant Administrative Officer posts. Graduates can apply online at licindia.in before 26 June 2026. Check eligibility details.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'UPSC CDS (II) 2026 – Combined Defence Services Examination', 'upsc-cds-ii-2026-combined-defence-services', 'UPSC has released the Combined Defence Services Examination (II) 2026 notification for admission to the Indian Military Academy, Indian Naval Academy, Air Force Academy and Officers Training Academy. Graduates can apply online at upsc.gov.in.', '<h2>UPSC CDS (II) 2026 – Combined Defence Services Examination – Complete Recruitment Overview</h2><p>The Union Public Service Commission has released the official notification for the recruitment to the post of <strong>UPSC CDS (II) 2026</strong>. This recruitment is a valuable opportunity for eligible candidates across the country to secure a stable and respectable government career with attractive pay, allowances, job security and excellent avenues for professional growth. Interested candidates who fulfil the prescribed eligibility conditions are advised to read the complete official notification carefully before submitting their online application on the official website https://upsc.gov.in.</p><h3>About the Post & Organisation</h3><p>The Union Public Service Commission conducts this recruitment to fill the post of UPSC CDS (II) 2026 through a transparent and merit-based selection process. The CDS examination is the gateway to a prestigious career as a commissioned officer in the Indian Armed Forces. The selected candidates will be entitled to the pay scale prescribed under the applicable pay matrix along with dearness allowance, house rent allowance, transport allowance and other admissible benefits as per the rules of the organisation. The post offers a structured career path with opportunities for promotion to higher grades based on seniority and departmental examinations.</p><h3>Important Dates</h3><ul><li>Notification Release: 20 May 2026</li><li>Application Start: 20 May 2026</li><li>Last Date to Apply: 9 June 2026</li><li>Written Examination: 6 September 2026 (Tentative)</li></ul><h3>Eligibility & Educational Qualification</h3><p>To be eligible for this recruitment, candidates must satisfy the educational qualification requirement, which is as follows: a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline for the Indian Military Academy and Officers Training Academy, a degree with Physics and Mathematics at the 10+2 level or a degree in Engineering for the Indian Naval Academy, and a degree with Physics and Mathematics at 10+2 or an Engineering degree for the Air Force Academy, from a recognized University. Candidates appearing in the final year of their degree examination are also eligible to apply provisionally, subject to producing proof of passing within the prescribed time. Candidates are strongly advised to verify that they meet all the prescribed academic and eligibility conditions as on the cut-off date mentioned in the official notification, since applications that do not meet the requirements are liable to be rejected at any stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>Age Limit & Relaxation</h3><p>The age limit prescribed for this recruitment is Approximately 19 to 25 years depending on the academy, as specified in the notification. Age relaxation is provided to candidates belonging to reserved categories as per the rules of the Government and the organisation, namely five years for SC and ST candidates, three years for OBC candidates, ten years for Persons with Benchmark Disabilities, and additional relaxation for Ex-Servicemen and other special categories as specified in the detailed notification.</p><h3>Application Fee</h3><p>The prescribed application fee must be paid online through net banking, debit card, credit card, UPI or other digital payment modes available on the portal. Candidates belonging to SC, ST, Persons with Disabilities, Ex-Servicemen and, in many cases, women candidates are eligible for fee exemption or a reduced fee as per the category-wise fee structure mentioned in the notification. Candidates should ensure that the fee is paid within the prescribed deadline, as applications without successful fee payment are treated as incomplete.</p><h3>Selection Process</h3><p>The selection process for this recruitment consists of a written examination conducted by UPSC, followed by an interview and personality test conducted by the Services Selection Board (SSB), and a medical examination.  The final merit list is prepared strictly on the basis of the candidate''''s performance in the prescribed stages, subject to document verification and fulfilment of all eligibility conditions. Candidates are advised to prepare thoroughly for each stage and to keep track of the official announcements regarding the examination schedule and results.</p><h3>How to Apply</h3><p>Eligible and interested candidates must apply online through the official website https://upsc.gov.in within the application window. The step-by-step procedure involves registering with a valid email address and mobile number, filling in the personal, educational and communication details, uploading the scanned photograph, signature and required documents in the prescribed format and size, paying the application fee, and finally submitting the completed application form. Candidates are advised to take a printout of the submitted application form and the fee receipt for future reference, and to avoid waiting until the last date to prevent any last-minute technical difficulties.</p>', 'Defence', 'UPSC', 'Union Public Service Commission', 'notification', '2026-05-20', '2026-05-20', '2026-05-20', '2026-06-09', '2026-06-09', '2026-09-06', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 453, 'Approximately 19 to 25 years depending on the academy, as specified in the notification', 'a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline for the Indian Military Academy and Officers Training Academy, a degree with Physics and Mathematics at the 10+2 level or a degree in Engineering for the Indian Naval Academy, and a degree with Physics and Mathematics at 10+2 or an Engineering degree for the Air Force Academy, from a recognized University', 'Candidates appearing in the final year of their degree examination are also eligible to apply provisionally, subject to producing proof of passing within the prescribed time.', 200.00, 200.00, 0.00, 'https://upsc.gov.in', 'https://upsc.gov.in', 'https://upsc.gov.in/sites/default/files/Notif-CDS-II-2026.pdf', 'https://upsconline.nic.in', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ACTIVE', 0, 1, 'UPSC CDS 2 2026 – Apply Online for Defence Services Posts', 'UPSC CDS (II) 2026 notification out for IMA, INA, AFA and OTA. Graduates can apply online at upsc.gov.in before 9 June 2026. Check eligibility and exam dates.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'AFCAT 02/2026 – Air Force Common Admission Test Notification', 'afcat-02-2026-air-force-common-admission-test', 'Indian Air Force has released the AFCAT 02/2026 notification for recruitment of officers in the Flying Branch and Ground Duty (Technical and Non-Technical) branches. Graduates can apply online at afcat.cdac.in.', '<h2>AFCAT 02/2026 – Air Force Common Admission Test Notification – Complete Recruitment Overview</h2><p>The Indian Air Force has released the official notification for the recruitment to the post of <strong>AFCAT 02/2026</strong>. This recruitment is a valuable opportunity for eligible candidates across the country to secure a stable and respectable government career with attractive pay, allowances, job security and excellent avenues for professional growth. Interested candidates who fulfil the prescribed eligibility conditions are advised to read the complete official notification carefully before submitting their online application on the official website https://afcat.cdac.in.</p><h3>About the Post & Organisation</h3><p>The Indian Air Force conducts this recruitment to fill the post of AFCAT 02/2026 through a transparent and merit-based selection process. A commission in the Indian Air Force offers an honourable and adventurous career with excellent pay and perks. The selected candidates will be entitled to the pay scale prescribed under the applicable pay matrix along with dearness allowance, house rent allowance, transport allowance and other admissible benefits as per the rules of the organisation. The post offers a structured career path with opportunities for promotion to higher grades based on seniority and departmental examinations.</p><h3>Important Dates</h3><ul><li>Notification Release: 1 June 2026</li><li>Application Start: 1 June 2026</li><li>Last Date to Apply: 30 June 2026</li><li>AFCAT Examination: August 2026 (Tentative)</li></ul><h3>Eligibility & Educational Qualification</h3><p>To be eligible for this recruitment, candidates must satisfy the educational qualification requirement, which is as follows: a graduation degree with a minimum of 60% marks for the Flying Branch (with Physics and Mathematics at 10+2), the relevant engineering degree for the Technical Branch, and a graduation or post-graduation degree in the prescribed disciplines for the Ground Duty Non-Technical Branch, from a recognized University. Candidates must meet the branch-specific educational requirements and the medical standards laid down by the Indian Air Force for the respective branch. Candidates are strongly advised to verify that they meet all the prescribed academic and eligibility conditions as on the cut-off date mentioned in the official notification, since applications that do not meet the requirements are liable to be rejected at any stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>Age Limit & Relaxation</h3><p>The age limit prescribed for this recruitment is 20 to 24 years for the Flying Branch and 20 to 26 years for the Ground Duty branches, as on the course commencement date. Age relaxation is provided to candidates belonging to reserved categories as per the rules of the Government and the organisation, namely five years for SC and ST candidates, three years for OBC candidates, ten years for Persons with Benchmark Disabilities, and additional relaxation for Ex-Servicemen and other special categories as specified in the detailed notification.</p><h3>Application Fee</h3><p>The prescribed application fee must be paid online through net banking, debit card, credit card, UPI or other digital payment modes available on the portal. Candidates belonging to SC, ST, Persons with Disabilities, Ex-Servicemen and, in many cases, women candidates are eligible for fee exemption or a reduced fee as per the category-wise fee structure mentioned in the notification. Candidates should ensure that the fee is paid within the prescribed deadline, as applications without successful fee payment are treated as incomplete.</p><h3>Selection Process</h3><p>The selection process for this recruitment consists of the online AFCAT examination (and the Engineering Knowledge Test for the Technical Branch), followed by the Air Force Selection Board testing, and a medical examination.  The final merit list is prepared strictly on the basis of the candidate''''s performance in the prescribed stages, subject to document verification and fulfilment of all eligibility conditions. Candidates are advised to prepare thoroughly for each stage and to keep track of the official announcements regarding the examination schedule and results.</p><h3>How to Apply</h3><p>Eligible and interested candidates must apply online through the official website https://afcat.cdac.in within the application window. The step-by-step procedure involves registering with a valid email address and mobile number, filling in the personal, educational and communication details, uploading the scanned photograph, signature and required documents in the prescribed format and size, paying the application fee, and finally submitting the completed application form. Candidates are advised to take a printout of the submitted application form and the fee receipt for future reference, and to avoid waiting until the last date to prevent any last-minute technical difficulties.</p>', 'Defence', 'Indian Air Force', 'Indian Air Force', 'notification', '2026-06-01', '2026-06-01', '2026-06-01', '2026-06-30', '2026-06-30', '2026-08-22', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 336, '20 to 24 years for the Flying Branch and 20 to 26 years for the Ground Duty branches, as on the course commencement date', 'a graduation degree with a minimum of 60% marks for the Flying Branch (with Physics and Mathematics at 10+2), the relevant engineering degree for the Technical Branch, and a graduation or post-graduation degree in the prescribed disciplines for the Ground Duty Non-Technical Branch, from a recognized University', 'Candidates must meet the branch-specific educational requirements and the medical standards laid down by the Indian Air Force for the respective branch.', 550.00, 550.00, 550.00, 'https://afcat.cdac.in', 'https://afcat.cdac.in', 'https://afcat.cdac.in/notifications/afcat-02-2026.pdf', 'https://afcat.cdac.in', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ACTIVE', 0, 1, 'AFCAT 02/2026 – Apply Online for Indian Air Force Officer Posts', 'AFCAT 02/2026 notification out for Flying and Ground Duty branches. Graduates can apply online at afcat.cdac.in before 30 June 2026. Check eligibility.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'SSC Stenographer Grade C & D 2026 Recruitment', 'ssc-stenographer-grade-c-d-2026', 'Staff Selection Commission has released the SSC Stenographer Grade C and Grade D 2026 notification for recruitment of stenographers in various central government ministries and departments. 12th pass candidates can apply online at ssc.gov.in.', '<h2>SSC Stenographer Grade C & D 2026 Recruitment – Complete Recruitment Overview</h2><p>The Staff Selection Commission has released the official notification for the recruitment to the post of <strong>SSC Stenographer Grade C & D 2026 Recruitment</strong>. This recruitment is a valuable opportunity for eligible candidates across the country to secure a stable and respectable government career with attractive pay, allowances, job security and excellent avenues for professional growth. Interested candidates who fulfil the prescribed eligibility conditions are advised to read the complete official notification carefully before submitting their online application on the official website https://ssc.gov.in.</p><h3>About the Post & Organisation</h3><p>The Staff Selection Commission conducts this recruitment to fill the post of SSC Stenographer Grade C & D 2026 Recruitment through a transparent and merit-based selection process. Stenographers play a key role in providing secretarial assistance to senior officers in government offices. The selected candidates will be entitled to the pay scale prescribed under the applicable pay matrix along with dearness allowance, house rent allowance, transport allowance and other admissible benefits as per the rules of the organisation. The post offers a structured career path with opportunities for promotion to higher grades based on seniority and departmental examinations.</p><h3>Important Dates</h3><ul><li>Notification Release: 12 June 2026</li><li>Application Start: 15 June 2026</li><li>Last Date to Apply: 10 July 2026</li><li>Computer Based Examination: October 2026 (Tentative)</li></ul><h3>Eligibility & Educational Qualification</h3><p>To be eligible for this recruitment, candidates must satisfy the educational qualification requirement, which is as follows: a pass in the 12th Standard (10+2) or equivalent examination from a recognized Board or University, along with proficiency in stenography. Candidates must possess skill in stenography, which is tested through a stenography skill test at the prescribed speed of 100 words per minute for Grade C and 80 words per minute for Grade D. Candidates are strongly advised to verify that they meet all the prescribed academic and eligibility conditions as on the cut-off date mentioned in the official notification, since applications that do not meet the requirements are liable to be rejected at any stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>Age Limit & Relaxation</h3><p>The age limit prescribed for this recruitment is 18 to 30 years for Grade C and 18 to 27 years for Grade D, with relaxation for reserved categories. Age relaxation is provided to candidates belonging to reserved categories as per the rules of the Government and the organisation, namely five years for SC and ST candidates, three years for OBC candidates, ten years for Persons with Benchmark Disabilities, and additional relaxation for Ex-Servicemen and other special categories as specified in the detailed notification.</p><h3>Application Fee</h3><p>The prescribed application fee must be paid online through net banking, debit card, credit card, UPI or other digital payment modes available on the portal. Candidates belonging to SC, ST, Persons with Disabilities, Ex-Servicemen and, in many cases, women candidates are eligible for fee exemption or a reduced fee as per the category-wise fee structure mentioned in the notification. Candidates should ensure that the fee is paid within the prescribed deadline, as applications without successful fee payment are treated as incomplete.</p><h3>Selection Process</h3><p>The selection process for this recruitment consists of a Computer Based Examination followed by a Skill Test in stenography and document verification.  The final merit list is prepared strictly on the basis of the candidate''''s performance in the prescribed stages, subject to document verification and fulfilment of all eligibility conditions. Candidates are advised to prepare thoroughly for each stage and to keep track of the official announcements regarding the examination schedule and results.</p><h3>How to Apply</h3><p>Eligible and interested candidates must apply online through the official website https://ssc.gov.in within the application window. The step-by-step procedure involves registering with a valid email address and mobile number, filling in the personal, educational and communication details, uploading the scanned photograph, signature and required documents in the prescribed format and size, paying the application fee, and finally submitting the completed application form. Candidates are advised to take a printout of the submitted application form and the fee receipt for future reference, and to avoid waiting until the last date to prevent any last-minute technical difficulties.</p>', 'Central Govt', 'SSC', 'Staff Selection Commission', 'notification', '2026-06-12', '2026-06-13', '2026-06-15', '2026-07-10', '2026-07-10', '2026-10-15', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 2006, '18 to 30 years for Grade C and 18 to 27 years for Grade D, with relaxation for reserved categories', 'a pass in the 12th Standard (10+2) or equivalent examination from a recognized Board or University, along with proficiency in stenography', 'Candidates must possess skill in stenography, which is tested through a stenography skill test at the prescribed speed of 100 words per minute for Grade C and 80 words per minute for Grade D.', 100.00, 100.00, 0.00, 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in/notifications/stenographer-2026.pdf', 'https://ssc.gov.in/portal/apply', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ACTIVE', 0, 1, 'SS