(NULL, 'KVS Recruitment 2026 – PRT, TGT & PGT Teaching Posts', 'kvs-recruitment-2026-prt-tgt-pgt', 'Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan has released the KVS Recruitment 2026 notification for Primary Teacher (PRT), Trained Graduate Teacher (TGT) and Post Graduate Teacher (PGT) posts. Eligible candidates can apply online at kvsangathan.nic.in.', '<h2>KVS Recruitment 2026 – PRT, TGT & PGT Teaching Posts – Complete Recruitment Overview</h2><p>The Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan has released the official notification for the recruitment to the post of <strong>KVS Recruitment 2026</strong>. This recruitment is a valuable opportunity for eligible candidates across the country to secure a stable and respectable government career with attractive pay, allowances, job security and excellent avenues for professional growth. Interested candidates who fulfil the prescribed eligibility conditions are advised to read the complete official notification carefully before submitting their online application on the official website https://kvsangathan.nic.in.</p><h3>About the Post & Organisation</h3><p>The Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan conducts this recruitment to fill the post of KVS Recruitment 2026 through a transparent and merit-based selection process. Kendriya Vidyalayas are among the most reputed schools in the country, offering teachers a prestigious and secure career. The selected candidates will be entitled to the pay scale prescribed under the applicable pay matrix along with dearness allowance, house rent allowance, transport allowance and other admissible benefits as per the rules of the organisation. The post offers a structured career path with opportunities for promotion to higher grades based on seniority and departmental examinations.</p><h3>Important Dates</h3><ul><li>Notification Release: 8 June 2026</li><li>Application Start: 12 June 2026</li><li>Last Date to Apply: 5 July 2026</li><li>Written Examination: September 2026 (Tentative)</li></ul><h3>Eligibility & Educational Qualification</h3><p>To be eligible for this recruitment, candidates must satisfy the educational qualification requirement, which is as follows: Senior Secondary with 50% and a two-year Diploma in Elementary Education along with CTET for PRT; a Bachelor''''s Degree with the relevant subject, B.Ed and CTET for TGT; and a Master''''s Degree in the relevant subject with B.Ed for PGT, from a recognized University. Candidates must possess the prescribed academic and professional teaching qualification for the respective post, along with proficiency in teaching in Hindi and English media as applicable. Candidates are strongly advised to verify that they meet all the prescribed academic and eligibility conditions as on the cut-off date mentioned in the official notification, since applications that do not meet the requirements are liable to be rejected at any stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>Age Limit & Relaxation</h3><p>The age limit prescribed for this recruitment is Up to 30 years for PRT, up to 35 years for TGT and up to 40 years for PGT, with relaxation for reserved categories. Age relaxation is provided to candidates belonging to reserved categories as per the rules of the Government and the organisation, namely five years for SC and ST candidates, three years for OBC candidates, ten years for Persons with Benchmark Disabilities, and additional relaxation for Ex-Servicemen and other special categories as specified in the detailed notification.</p><h3>Application Fee</h3><p>The prescribed application fee must be paid online through net banking, debit card, credit card, UPI or other digital payment modes available on the portal. Candidates belonging to SC, ST, Persons with Disabilities, Ex-Servicemen and, in many cases, women candidates are eligible for fee exemption or a reduced fee as per the category-wise fee structure mentioned in the notification. Candidates should ensure that the fee is paid within the prescribed deadline, as applications without successful fee payment are treated as incomplete.</p><h3>Selection Process</h3><p>The selection process for this recruitment consists of a written examination, followed by an interview and document verification for the relevant posts.  The final merit list is prepared strictly on the basis of the candidate''''s performance in the prescribed stages, subject to document verification and fulfilment of all eligibility conditions. Candidates are advised to prepare thoroughly for each stage and to keep track of the official announcements regarding the examination schedule and results.</p><h3>How to Apply</h3><p>Eligible and interested candidates must apply online through the official website https://kvsangathan.nic.in within the application window. The step-by-step procedure involves registering with a valid email address and mobile number, filling in the personal, educational and communication details, uploading the scanned photograph, signature and required documents in the prescribed format and size, paying the application fee, and finally submitting the completed application form. Candidates are advised to take a printout of the submitted application form and the fee receipt for future reference, and to avoid waiting until the last date to prevent any last-minute technical difficulties.</p>', 'Teaching', 'KVS', 'Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan', 'notification', '2026-06-08', '2026-06-09', '2026-06-12', '2026-07-05', '2026-07-05', '2026-09-15', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 6745, 'Up to 30 years for PRT, up to 35 years for TGT and up to 40 years for PGT, with relaxation for reserved categories', 'Senior Secondary with 50% and a two-year Diploma in Elementary Education along with CTET for PRT; a Bachelor''''s Degree with the relevant subject, B.Ed and CTET for TGT; and a Master''''s Degree in the relevant subject with B.Ed for PGT, from a recognized University', 'Candidates must possess the prescribed academic and professional teaching qualification for the respective post, along with proficiency in teaching in Hindi and English media as applicable.', 1500.00, 1500.00, 0.00, 'https://kvsangathan.nic.in', 'https://kvsangathan.nic.in', 'https://kvsangathan.nic.in/notifications/recruitment-2026.pdf', 'https://kvsangathan.nic.in', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ACTIVE', 1, 1, 'KVS Recruitment 2026 – Apply Online for PRT TGT PGT Teaching Posts', 'KVS Recruitment 2026 for PRT, TGT and PGT teaching posts. Eligible candidates can apply online at kvsangathan.nic.in before 5 July 2026. Check eligibility.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'ESIC UDC 2026 – Upper Division Clerk Recruitment', 'esic-udc-2026-upper-division-clerk', 'Employees State Insurance Corporation has released the ESIC UDC 2026 notification for recruitment of Upper Division Clerks in various regional and sub-regional offices. Graduates can apply online at esic.gov.in.', '<h2>ESIC UDC 2026 – Upper Division Clerk Recruitment – Complete Recruitment Overview</h2><p>The Employees State Insurance Corporation has released the official notification for the recruitment to the post of <strong>ESIC UDC 2026</strong>. This recruitment is a valuable opportunity for eligible candidates across the country to secure a stable and respectable government career with attractive pay, allowances, job security and excellent avenues for professional growth. Interested candidates who fulfil the prescribed eligibility conditions are advised to read the complete official notification carefully before submitting their online application on the official website https://www.esic.gov.in.</p><h3>About the Post & Organisation</h3><p>The Employees State Insurance Corporation conducts this recruitment to fill the post of ESIC UDC 2026 through a transparent and merit-based selection process. ESIC provides social security and health insurance to workers, and the UDC post offers a stable central government career. The selected candidates will be entitled to the pay scale prescribed under the applicable pay matrix along with dearness allowance, house rent allowance, transport allowance and other admissible benefits as per the rules of the organisation. The post offers a structured career path with opportunities for promotion to higher grades based on seniority and departmental examinations.</p><h3>Important Dates</h3><ul><li>Notification Release: 6 June 2026</li><li>Application Start: 10 June 2026</li><li>Last Date to Apply: 8 July 2026</li><li>Preliminary Examination: September 2026 (Tentative)</li></ul><h3>Eligibility & Educational Qualification</h3><p>To be eligible for this recruitment, candidates must satisfy the educational qualification requirement, which is as follows: a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline from a recognized University, along with a working knowledge of computers including the use of office suites and databases. Candidates must possess computer proficiency, and knowledge of the regional language of the office to which they are applying is desirable for effective performance of duties. Candidates are strongly advised to verify that they meet all the prescribed academic and eligibility conditions as on the cut-off date mentioned in the official notification, since applications that do not meet the requirements are liable to be rejected at any stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>Age Limit & Relaxation</h3><p>The age limit prescribed for this recruitment is 18 to 27 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories. Age relaxation is provided to candidates belonging to reserved categories as per the rules of the Government and the organisation, namely five years for SC and ST candidates, three years for OBC candidates, ten years for Persons with Benchmark Disabilities, and additional relaxation for Ex-Servicemen and other special categories as specified in the detailed notification.</p><h3>Application Fee</h3><p>The prescribed application fee must be paid online through net banking, debit card, credit card, UPI or other digital payment modes available on the portal. Candidates belonging to SC, ST, Persons with Disabilities, Ex-Servicemen and, in many cases, women candidates are eligible for fee exemption or a reduced fee as per the category-wise fee structure mentioned in the notification. Candidates should ensure that the fee is paid within the prescribed deadline, as applications without successful fee payment are treated as incomplete.</p><h3>Selection Process</h3><p>The selection process for this recruitment consists of a Phase-I preliminary examination, a Phase-II main examination, and a computer skill test.  The final merit list is prepared strictly on the basis of the candidate''''s performance in the prescribed stages, subject to document verification and fulfilment of all eligibility conditions. Candidates are advised to prepare thoroughly for each stage and to keep track of the official announcements regarding the examination schedule and results.</p><h3>How to Apply</h3><p>Eligible and interested candidates must apply online through the official website https://www.esic.gov.in within the application window. The step-by-step procedure involves registering with a valid email address and mobile number, filling in the personal, educational and communication details, uploading the scanned photograph, signature and required documents in the prescribed format and size, paying the application fee, and finally submitting the completed application form. Candidates are advised to take a printout of the submitted application form and the fee receipt for future reference, and to avoid waiting until the last date to prevent any last-minute technical difficulties.</p>', 'Central Govt', 'ESIC', 'Employees State Insurance Corporation', 'notification', '2026-06-06', '2026-06-07', '2026-06-10', '2026-07-08', '2026-07-08', '2026-09-12', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 1500, '18 to 27 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories', 'a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline from a recognized University, along with a working knowledge of computers including the use of office suites and databases', 'Candidates must possess computer proficiency, and knowledge of the regional language of the office to which they are applying is desirable for effective performance of duties.', 500.00, 500.00, 250.00, 'https://www.esic.gov.in', 'https://www.esic.gov.in', 'https://www.esic.gov.in/notifications/udc-2026.pdf', 'https://www.esic.gov.in/recruitments', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ACTIVE', 0, 1, 'ESIC UDC 2026 – Apply Online for Upper Division Clerk Posts', 'ESIC UDC 2026 recruitment for Upper Division Clerk posts. Graduates with computer knowledge can apply online at esic.gov.in before 8 July 2026.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'ONGC Non-Executive 2026 – Technician & Assistant Recruitment', 'ongc-non-executive-2026-technician-assistant', 'Oil and Natural Gas Corporation has released the ONGC Non-Executive 2026 notification for recruitment to various technician, assistant and junior posts through GATE and trade-based selection. Eligible candidates can apply online at ongcindia.com.', '<h2>ONGC Non-Executive 2026 – Technician & Assistant Recruitment – Complete Recruitment Overview</h2><p>The Oil and Natural Gas Corporation has released the official notification for the recruitment to the post of <strong>ONGC Non-Executive 2026</strong>. This recruitment is a valuable opportunity for eligible candidates across the country to secure a stable and respectable government career with attractive pay, allowances, job security and excellent avenues for professional growth. Interested candidates who fulfil the prescribed eligibility conditions are advised to read the complete official notification carefully before submitting their online application on the official website https://ongcindia.com.</p><h3>About the Post & Organisation</h3><p>The Oil and Natural Gas Corporation conducts this recruitment to fill the post of ONGC Non-Executive 2026 through a transparent and merit-based selection process. ONGC is a Maharatna public sector enterprise and one of the most sought-after employers in the energy sector. The selected candidates will be entitled to the pay scale prescribed under the applicable pay matrix along with dearness allowance, house rent allowance, transport allowance and other admissible benefits as per the rules of the organisation. The post offers a structured career path with opportunities for promotion to higher grades based on seniority and departmental examinations.</p><h3>Important Dates</h3><ul><li>Notification Release: 10 June 2026</li><li>Application Start: 12 June 2026</li><li>Last Date to Apply: 2 July 2026</li><li>Computer Based Test: September 2026 (Tentative)</li></ul><h3>Eligibility & Educational Qualification</h3><p>To be eligible for this recruitment, candidates must satisfy the educational qualification requirement, which is as follows: the relevant Diploma in Engineering, ITI certificate, or graduation degree depending on the post, from a recognized Board, institute or University as specified in the official advertisement. Candidates must possess the exact qualification mentioned for each post code, and for certain posts the selection is based on the valid GATE score in the relevant discipline. Candidates are strongly advised to verify that they meet all the prescribed academic and eligibility conditions as on the cut-off date mentioned in the official notification, since applications that do not meet the requirements are liable to be rejected at any stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>Age Limit & Relaxation</h3><p>The age limit prescribed for this recruitment is 18 to 30 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories. Age relaxation is provided to candidates belonging to reserved categories as per the rules of the Government and the organisation, namely five years for SC and ST candidates, three years for OBC candidates, ten years for Persons with Benchmark Disabilities, and additional relaxation for Ex-Servicemen and other special categories as specified in the detailed notification.</p><h3>Application Fee</h3><p>The prescribed application fee must be paid online through net banking, debit card, credit card, UPI or other digital payment modes available on the portal. Candidates belonging to SC, ST, Persons with Disabilities, Ex-Servicemen and, in many cases, women candidates are eligible for fee exemption or a reduced fee as per the category-wise fee structure mentioned in the notification. Candidates should ensure that the fee is paid within the prescribed deadline, as applications without successful fee payment are treated as incomplete.</p><h3>Selection Process</h3><p>The selection process for this recruitment consists of either a Computer Based Test or selection on the basis of a valid GATE score, followed by a physical efficiency test, skill test and document verification as applicable to the post.  The final merit list is prepared strictly on the basis of the candidate''''s performance in the prescribed stages, subject to document verification and fulfilment of all eligibility conditions. Candidates are advised to prepare thoroughly for each stage and to keep track of the official announcements regarding the examination schedule and results.</p><h3>How to Apply</h3><p>Eligible and interested candidates must apply online through the official website https://ongcindia.com within the application window. The step-by-step procedure involves registering with a valid email address and mobile number, filling in the personal, educational and communication details, uploading the scanned photograph, signature and required documents in the prescribed format and size, paying the application fee, and finally submitting the completed application form. Candidates are advised to take a printout of the submitted application form and the fee receipt for future reference, and to avoid waiting until the last date to prevent any last-minute technical difficulties.</p>', 'PSU', 'ONGC', 'Oil and Natural Gas Corporation', 'notification', '2026-06-10', '2026-06-11', '2026-06-12', '2026-07-02', '2026-07-02', '2026-09-10', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 2200, '18 to 30 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories', 'the relevant Diploma in Engineering, ITI certificate, or graduation degree depending on the post, from a recognized Board, institute or University as specified in the official advertisement', 'Candidates must possess the exact qualification mentioned for each post code, and for certain posts the selection is based on the valid GATE score in the relevant discipline.', 370.00, 370.00, 0.00, 'https://ongcindia.com', 'https://ongcindia.com', 'https://ongcindia.com/notifications/non-executive-2026.pdf', 'https://ongcindia.com/careers', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ACTIVE', 0, 1, 'ONGC Non-Executive 2026 – Apply Online for Technician & Assistant Posts', 'ONGC Non-Executive 2026 recruitment for technician and assistant posts via GATE and CBT. Apply online at ongcindia.com before 2 July 2026.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'DSSSB Recruitment 2026 – Multiple Posts in Delhi Government', 'dsssb-recruitment-2026-multiple-posts', 'Delhi Subordinate Services Selection Board has released the DSSSB Recruitment 2026 notification for various posts including Junior Assistant, Patwari, Teacher and technical posts under the Government of NCT of Delhi. Eligible candidates can apply online at dsssb.delhi.gov.in.', '<h2>DSSSB Recruitment 2026 – Multiple Posts in Delhi Government – Complete Recruitment Overview</h2><p>The Delhi Subordinate Services Selection Board has released the official notification for the recruitment to the post of <strong>DSSSB Recruitment 2026</strong>. This recruitment is a valuable opportunity for eligible candidates across the country to secure a stable and respectable government career with attractive pay, allowances, job security and excellent avenues for professional growth. Interested candidates who fulfil the prescribed eligibility conditions are advised to read the complete official notification carefully before submitting their online application on the official website https://dsssb.delhi.gov.in.</p><h3>About the Post & Organisation</h3><p>The Delhi Subordinate Services Selection Board conducts this recruitment to fill the post of DSSSB Recruitment 2026 through a transparent and merit-based selection process. DSSSB recruits for a wide range of departments under the Delhi Government, offering candidates diverse career opportunities. The selected candidates will be entitled to the pay scale prescribed under the applicable pay matrix along with dearness allowance, house rent allowance, transport allowance and other admissible benefits as per the rules of the organisation. The post offers a structured career path with opportunities for promotion to higher grades based on seniority and departmental examinations.</p><h3>Important Dates</h3><ul><li>Notification Release: 9 June 2026</li><li>Application Start: 12 June 2026</li><li>Last Date to Apply: 11 July 2026</li><li>Computer Based Examination: October 2026 (Tentative)</li></ul><h3>Eligibility & Educational Qualification</h3><p>To be eligible for this recruitment, candidates must satisfy the educational qualification requirement, which is as follows: 10th, 12th, graduation or post-graduation along with the relevant professional or technical qualification depending on the post applied for, from a recognized Board, institute or University. Candidates must possess the exact educational and professional qualification prescribed for each post code, and certain posts additionally require a typing test or teaching qualification such as B.Ed and CTET. Candidates are strongly advised to verify that they meet all the prescribed academic and eligibility conditions as on the cut-off date mentioned in the official notification, since applications that do not meet the requirements are liable to be rejected at any stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>Age Limit & Relaxation</h3><p>The age limit prescribed for this recruitment is 18 to 32 years depending on the post, with relaxation for reserved categories. Age relaxation is provided to candidates belonging to reserved categories as per the rules of the Government and the organisation, namely five years for SC and ST candidates, three years for OBC candidates, ten years for Persons with Benchmark Disabilities, and additional relaxation for Ex-Servicemen and other special categories as specified in the detailed notification.</p><h3>Application Fee</h3><p>The prescribed application fee must be paid online through net banking, debit card, credit card, UPI or other digital payment modes available on the portal. Candidates belonging to SC, ST, Persons with Disabilities, Ex-Servicemen and, in many cases, women candidates are eligible for fee exemption or a reduced fee as per the category-wise fee structure mentioned in the notification. Candidates should ensure that the fee is paid within the prescribed deadline, as applications without successful fee payment are treated as incomplete.</p><h3>Selection Process</h3><p>The selection process for this recruitment consists of a one-tier or two-tier Computer Based Examination, followed by a skill test or teaching aptitude test for the relevant posts and document verification.  The final merit list is prepared strictly on the basis of the candidate''''s performance in the prescribed stages, subject to document verification and fulfilment of all eligibility conditions. Candidates are advised to prepare thoroughly for each stage and to keep track of the official announcements regarding the examination schedule and results.</p><h3>How to Apply</h3><p>Eligible and interested candidates must apply online through the official website https://dsssb.delhi.gov.in within the application window. The step-by-step procedure involves registering with a valid email address and mobile number, filling in the personal, educational and communication details, uploading the scanned photograph, signature and required documents in the prescribed format and size, paying the application fee, and finally submitting the completed application form. Candidates are advised to take a printout of the submitted application form and the fee receipt for future reference, and to avoid waiting until the last date to prevent any last-minute technical difficulties.</p>', 'State Govt', 'DSSSB', 'Delhi Subordinate Services Selection Board', 'notification', '2026-06-09', '2026-06-10', '2026-06-12', '2026-07-11', '2026-07-11', '2026-10-18', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 5500, '18 to 32 years depending on the post, with relaxation for reserved categories', '10th, 12th, graduation or post-graduation along with the relevant professional or technical qualification depending on the post applied for, from a recognized Board, institute or University', 'Candidates must possess the exact educational and professional qualification prescribed for each post code, and certain posts additionally require a typing test or teaching qualification such as B.Ed and CTET.', 100.00, 100.00, 0.00, 'https://dsssb.delhi.gov.in', 'https://dsssb.delhi.gov.in', 'https://dsssb.delhi.gov.in/notifications/recruitment-2026.pdf', 'https://dsssbonline.nic.in', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ACTIVE', 0, 1, 'DSSSB Recruitment 2026 – Apply Online for Delhi Government Posts', 'DSSSB Recruitment 2026 for various Delhi Government posts. Eligible candidates can apply online at dsssb.delhi.gov.in before 11 July 2026. Check eligibility.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'RRB JE 2026 – Junior Engineer & Technical Posts Recruitment', 'rrb-je-2026-junior-engineer-recruitment', 'Railway Recruitment Boards have released the RRB Junior Engineer (JE) 2026 notification for recruitment of Junior Engineers, Depot Material Superintendents and Chemical & Metallurgical Assistants in Indian Railways. Diploma and degree holders can apply online at rrbcdg.gov.in.', '<h2>RRB JE 2026 – Junior Engineer & Technical Posts Recruitment – Complete Recruitment Overview</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Boards has released the official notification for the recruitment to the post of <strong>RRB JE 2026</strong>. This recruitment is a valuable opportunity for eligible candidates across the country to secure a stable and respectable government career with attractive pay, allowances, job security and excellent avenues for professional growth. Interested candidates who fulfil the prescribed eligibility conditions are advised to read the complete official notification carefully before submitting their online application on the official website https://rrbcdg.gov.in.</p><h3>About the Post & Organisation</h3><p>The Railway Recruitment Boards conducts this recruitment to fill the post of RRB JE 2026 through a transparent and merit-based selection process. The Junior Engineer post offers a respectable technical career in Indian Railways with Pay Level 6 and good growth prospects. The selected candidates will be entitled to the pay scale prescribed under the applicable pay matrix along with dearness allowance, house rent allowance, transport allowance and other admissible benefits as per the rules of the organisation. The post offers a structured career path with opportunities for promotion to higher grades based on seniority and departmental examinations.</p><h3>Important Dates</h3><ul><li>Notification Release: 7 June 2026</li><li>Application Start: 12 June 2026</li><li>Last Date to Apply: 11 July 2026</li><li>CBT-1 Examination: October 2026 (Tentative)</li></ul><h3>Eligibility & Educational Qualification</h3><p>To be eligible for this recruitment, candidates must satisfy the educational qualification requirement, which is as follows: a three-year Diploma or a Degree in the relevant Engineering discipline such as Civil, Mechanical, Electrical, Electronics or Computer Science from a recognized institution or University, depending on the post and exam group. Candidates must hold the exact engineering qualification prescribed for the post and exam group for which they apply, as listed in the official notification. Candidates are strongly advised to verify that they meet all the prescribed academic and eligibility conditions as on the cut-off date mentioned in the official notification, since applications that do not meet the requirements are liable to be rejected at any stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>Age Limit & Relaxation</h3><p>The age limit prescribed for this recruitment is 18 to 36 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories. Age relaxation is provided to candidates belonging to reserved categories as per the rules of the Government and the organisation, namely five years for SC and ST candidates, three years for OBC candidates, ten years for Persons with Benchmark Disabilities, and additional relaxation for Ex-Servicemen and other special categories as specified in the detailed notification.</p><h3>Application Fee</h3><p>The prescribed application fee must be paid online through net banking, debit card, credit card, UPI or other digital payment modes available on the portal. Candidates belonging to SC, ST, Persons with Disabilities, Ex-Servicemen and, in many cases, women candidates are eligible for fee exemption or a reduced fee as per the category-wise fee structure mentioned in the notification. Candidates should ensure that the fee is paid within the prescribed deadline, as applications without successful fee payment are treated as incomplete.</p><h3>Selection Process</h3><p>The selection process for this recruitment consists of a First Stage Computer Based Test (CBT-1), a Second Stage Computer Based Test (CBT-2), and document verification followed by a medical examination.  The final merit list is prepared strictly on the basis of the candidate''''s performance in the prescribed stages, subject to document verification and fulfilment of all eligibility conditions. Candidates are advised to prepare thoroughly for each stage and to keep track of the official announcements regarding the examination schedule and results.</p><h3>How to Apply</h3><p>Eligible and interested candidates must apply online through the official website https://rrbcdg.gov.in within the application window. The step-by-step procedure involves registering with a valid email address and mobile number, filling in the personal, educational and communication details, uploading the scanned photograph, signature and required documents in the prescribed format and size, paying the application fee, and finally submitting the completed application form. Candidates are advised to take a printout of the submitted application form and the fee receipt for future reference, and to avoid waiting until the last date to prevent any last-minute technical difficulties.</p>', 'Railways', 'RRB', 'Railway Recruitment Boards', 'notification', '2026-06-07', '2026-06-08', '2026-06-12', '2026-07-11', '2026-07-11', '2026-10-25', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 7951, '18 to 36 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories', 'a three-year Diploma or a Degree in the relevant Engineering discipline such as Civil, Mechanical, Electrical, Electronics or Computer Science from a recognized institution or University, depending on the post and exam group', 'Candidates must hold the exact engineering qualification prescribed for the post and exam group for which they apply, as listed in the official notification.', 500.00, 500.00, 250.00, 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in', 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in', 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in/notifications/je-2026.pdf', 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in/je-apply', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ACTIVE', 0, 1, 'RRB JE 2026 – Apply Online for Junior Engineer Posts at rrbcdg.gov.in', 'RRB JE 2026 recruitment for Junior Engineer and technical posts. Diploma/degree holders can apply online at rrbcdg.gov.in before 11 July 2026.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'UPSC CDS (II) 2026 Admit Card – Download e-Admit Card', 'upsc-cds-ii-2026-admit-card', 'UPSC has released the CDS (II) 2026 admit card. Candidates appearing in the Combined Defence Services Examination can download their e-admit card from upsc.gov.in using their registration ID or roll number.', '<h2>UPSC CDS (II) 2026 Admit Card – Download e-Admit Card</h2><p>The Union Public Service Commission has released the <strong>admit card</strong> for the UPSC CDS (II) 2026 Admit Card examination on its official website https://upsc.gov.in. The admit card, also known as the call letter or hall ticket, is one of the most important documents that every candidate must carry to the examination centre, since no candidate is permitted to enter the examination hall without a valid printed admit card and a matching original photo identity proof. Candidates who successfully submitted their applications can now download their admit card by logging in with their credentials.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Union Public Service Commission as part of the selection process for the post of UPSC CDS (II) 2026 Admit Card. The CDS examination selects candidates for officer training in the Indian Armed Forces academies. The admit card contains essential information such as the candidate''''s name, roll number, registration number, photograph, signature, examination date, reporting time, shift, and the complete address of the allotted examination centre, along with detailed instructions that every candidate must read and follow carefully on the day of the examination.</p><h3>How to Download the Admit Card</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://upsc.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the admit card or call letter download link for UPSC CDS (II) 2026 Admit Card.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password as applicable.</li><li>The admit card will be displayed on the screen with all your examination details.</li><li>Verify the details, download the admit card and take a clear printout on A4 size paper.</li></ol><h3>Documents to Carry</h3><p>Candidates must carry the printed copy of the admit card along with at least one original valid photo identity proof such as Aadhaar Card, Voter ID, PAN Card, Driving Licence or Passport. A recent passport-size colour photograph identical to the one uploaded during the application must also be carried and affixed where required. Candidates who fail to bring these documents will not be allowed to appear in the examination under any circumstances.</p><h3>Important Instructions</h3><p>Candidates are advised to reach the examination centre well before the reporting time indicated on the admit card, as late entry is strictly prohibited. Biometric verification, frisking and document checks are carried out at the centre and may take considerable time. Electronic gadgets including mobile phones, calculators, smartwatches, Bluetooth devices, and any printed or written study material are strictly banned inside the examination hall. Candidates must carefully verify every detail printed on the admit card and immediately report any discrepancy to the conducting authority.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates who meet the prescribed qualification, namely a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline for IMA and OTA, and a degree with Physics and Mathematics or an Engineering degree for the Naval and Air Force academies, from a recognized University. Only candidates whose applications were accepted by the Commission are issued the admit card for the written examination. The age criterion for the post is approximately 19 to 25 years depending on the academy. Candidates appearing in the examination should ensure that they continue to satisfy all eligibility conditions, as these are verified during the document verification stage that follows the written examination.</p><h3>Selection Process & Next Steps</h3><p>The overall selection for this recruitment consists of a written examination by UPSC, an SSB interview and a medical examination.  After appearing in the examination for which this admit card is issued, candidates should regularly monitor the official website https://upsc.gov.in for the answer key, result and the schedule of subsequent stages. It is advisable to retain the admit card safely even after the examination, as it is often required at later stages such as document verification and counselling.</p>', 'Defence', 'UPSC', 'Union Public Service Commission', 'admitcard', '2026-05-20', '2026-08-22', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-06', '2026-08-22', NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 453, 'approximately 19 to 25 years depending on the academy', 'a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline for IMA and OTA, and a degree with Physics and Mathematics or an Engineering degree for the Naval and Air Force academies, from a recognized University', 'Only candidates whose applications were accepted by the Commission are issued the admit card for the written examination.', 200.00, 200.00, 0.00, 'https://upsc.gov.in', 'https://upsc.gov.in', 'https://upsc.gov.in/sites/default/files/CDS-II-2026-Admit.pdf', 'https://upsc.gov.in/admit-card', NULL, NULL, 'admitcard', 'ADMIT_CARD', 0, 1, 'UPSC CDS 2 2026 Admit Card – Download at upsc.gov.in', 'UPSC CDS (II) 2026 admit card released. Download e-admit card at upsc.gov.in using registration ID or roll number. Written exam on 6 September 2026.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'AFCAT 02/2026 Admit Card – Download Air Force Hall Ticket', 'afcat-02-2026-admit-card', 'Indian Air Force has released the AFCAT 02/2026 admit card. Candidates can download their hall ticket from afcat.cdac.in using their login credentials. The online AFCAT examination is scheduled accordingly.', '<h2>AFCAT 02/2026 Admit Card – Download Air Force Hall Ticket</h2><p>The Indian Air Force has released the <strong>admit card</strong> for the AFCAT 02/2026 Admit Card examination on its official website https://afcat.cdac.in. The admit card, also known as the call letter or hall ticket, is one of the most important documents that every candidate must carry to the examination centre, since no candidate is permitted to enter the examination hall without a valid printed admit card and a matching original photo identity proof. Candidates who successfully submitted their applications can now download their admit card by logging in with their credentials.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Indian Air Force as part of the selection process for the post of AFCAT 02/2026 Admit Card. AFCAT is the entry test for a commissioned officer career in the Indian Air Force. The admit card contains essential information such as the candidate''''s name, roll number, registration number, photograph, signature, examination date, reporting time, shift, and the complete address of the allotted examination centre, along with detailed instructions that every candidate must read and follow carefully on the day of the examination.</p><h3>How to Download the Admit Card</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://afcat.cdac.in.</li><li>Click on the admit card or call letter download link for AFCAT 02/2026 Admit Card.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password as applicable.</li><li>The admit card will be displayed on the screen with all your examination details.</li><li>Verify the details, download the admit card and take a clear printout on A4 size paper.</li></ol><h3>Documents to Carry</h3><p>Candidates must carry the printed copy of the admit card along with at least one original valid photo identity proof such as Aadhaar Card, Voter ID, PAN Card, Driving Licence or Passport. A recent passport-size colour photograph identical to the one uploaded during the application must also be carried and affixed where required. Candidates who fail to bring these documents will not be allowed to appear in the examination under any circumstances.</p><h3>Important Instructions</h3><p>Candidates are advised to reach the examination centre well before the reporting time indicated on the admit card, as late entry is strictly prohibited. Biometric verification, frisking and document checks are carried out at the centre and may take considerable time. Electronic gadgets including mobile phones, calculators, smartwatches, Bluetooth devices, and any printed or written study material are strictly banned inside the examination hall. Candidates must carefully verify every detail printed on the admit card and immediately report any discrepancy to the conducting authority.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates who meet the prescribed qualification, namely a graduation degree with the prescribed marks for the Flying Branch, and the relevant engineering or graduation/post-graduation degree for the Technical and Ground Duty branches, from a recognized University. Candidates who registered and paid the fee for AFCAT 02/2026 can download the admit card for the online examination. The age criterion for the post is 20 to 24 years for the Flying Branch and 20 to 26 years for the Ground Duty branches. Candidates appearing in the examination should ensure that they continue to satisfy all eligibility conditions, as these are verified during the document verification stage that follows the written examination.</p><h3>Selection Process & Next Steps</h3><p>The overall selection for this recruitment consists of the online AFCAT examination, Air Force Selection Board testing and a medical examination.  After appearing in the examination for which this admit card is issued, candidates should regularly monitor the official website https://afcat.cdac.in for the answer key, result and the schedule of subsequent stages. It is advisable to retain the admit card safely even after the examination, as it is often required at later stages such as document verification and counselling.</p>', 'Defence', 'Indian Air Force', 'Indian Air Force', 'admitcard', '2026-06-01', '2026-08-15', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-22', '2026-08-15', NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 336, '20 to 24 years for the Flying Branch and 20 to 26 years for the Ground Duty branches', 'a graduation degree with the prescribed marks for the Flying Branch, and the relevant engineering or graduation/post-graduation degree for the Technical and Ground Duty branches, from a recognized University', 'Candidates who registered and paid the fee for AFCAT 02/2026 can download the admit card for the online examination.', 550.00, 550.00, 550.00, 'https://afcat.cdac.in', 'https://afcat.cdac.in', 'https://afcat.cdac.in/admit-card-02-2026.pdf', 'https://afcat.cdac.in', NULL, NULL, 'admitcard', 'ADMIT_CARD', 0, 1, 'AFCAT 02/2026 Admit Card – Download Hall Ticket at afcat.cdac.in', 'AFCAT 02/2026 admit card released. Download Indian Air Force hall ticket at afcat.cdac.in using login credentials. Check exam date and instructions.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'RBI Grade B 2026 Phase-I Admit Card – Download Call Letter', 'rbi-grade-b-2026-phase-1-admit-card', 'Reserve Bank of India has released the Grade B Officer 2026 Phase-I admit card. Candidates can download their call letter from rbi.org.in using their registration number and password.', '<h2>RBI Grade B 2026 Phase-I Admit Card – Download Call Letter</h2><p>The Reserve Bank of India has released the <strong>admit card</strong> for the RBI Grade B 2026 Phase-I Admit Card examination on its official website https://www.rbi.org.in. The admit card, also known as the call letter or hall ticket, is one of the most important documents that every candidate must carry to the examination centre, since no candidate is permitted to enter the examination hall without a valid printed admit card and a matching original photo identity proof. Candidates who successfully submitted their applications can now download their admit card by logging in with their credentials.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Reserve Bank of India as part of the selection process for the post of RBI Grade B 2026 Phase-I Admit Card. The Grade B Officer is a prestigious managerial post in the country''''s central bank. The admit card contains essential information such as the candidate''''s name, roll number, registration number, photograph, signature, examination date, reporting time, shift, and the complete address of the allotted examination centre, along with detailed instructions that every candidate must read and follow carefully on the day of the examination.</p><h3>How to Download the Admit Card</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://www.rbi.org.in.</li><li>Click on the admit card or call letter download link for RBI Grade B 2026 Phase-I Admit Card.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password as applicable.</li><li>The admit card will be displayed on the screen with all your examination details.</li><li>Verify the details, download the admit card and take a clear printout on A4 size paper.</li></ol><h3>Documents to Carry</h3><p>Candidates must carry the printed copy of the admit card along with at least one original valid photo identity proof such as Aadhaar Card, Voter ID, PAN Card, Driving Licence or Passport. A recent passport-size colour photograph identical to the one uploaded during the application must also be carried and affixed where required. Candidates who fail to bring these documents will not be allowed to appear in the examination under any circumstances.</p><h3>Important Instructions</h3><p>Candidates are advised to reach the examination centre well before the reporting time indicated on the admit card, as late entry is strictly prohibited. Biometric verification, frisking and document checks are carried out at the centre and may take considerable time. Electronic gadgets including mobile phones, calculators, smartwatches, Bluetooth devices, and any printed or written study material are strictly banned inside the examination hall. Candidates must carefully verify every detail printed on the admit card and immediately report any discrepancy to the conducting authority.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates who meet the prescribed qualification, namely a Bachelor''''s Degree with at least 60% marks for the General stream, or a Master''''s Degree in Economics or Statistics for the DEPR and DSIM streams, from a recognized University. Candidates who successfully registered for the Grade B 2026 recruitment can download the Phase-I online examination call letter. The age criterion for the post is 21 to 30 years as on the cut-off date. Candidates appearing in the examination should ensure that they continue to satisfy all eligibility conditions, as these are verified during the document verification stage that follows the written examination.</p><h3>Selection Process & Next Steps</h3><p>The overall selection for this recruitment consists of a Phase-I preliminary examination, a Phase-II main examination and an interview.  After appearing in the examination for which this admit card is issued, candidates should regularly monitor the official website https://www.rbi.org.in for the answer key, result and the schedule of subsequent stages. It is advisable to retain the admit card safely even after the examination, as it is often required at later stages such as document verification and counselling.</p>', 'Bank', 'RBI', 'Reserve Bank of India', 'admitcard', '2026-06-10', '2026-08-05', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-15', '2026-08-05', NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 94, '21 to 30 years as on the cut-off date', 'a Bachelor''''s Degree with at least 60% marks for the General stream, or a Master''''s Degree in Economics or Statistics for the DEPR and DSIM streams, from a recognized University', 'Candidates who successfully registered for the Grade B 2026 recruitment can download the Phase-I online examination call letter.', 850.00, 850.00, 100.00, 'https://www.rbi.org.in', 'https://www.rbi.org.in', 'https://opportunities.rbi.org.in/grade-b-2026-admit.pdf', 'https://opportunities.rbi.org.in', NULL, NULL, 'admitcard', 'ADMIT_CARD', 0, 1, 'RBI Grade B 2026 Phase-I Admit Card – Download at rbi.org.in', 'RBI Grade B Officer 2026 Phase-I admit card released. Download call letter at rbi.org.in using registration number and password. Check exam details.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
