(NULL, 'RRB Group D 2026 CBT Admit Card – Download Hall Ticket', 'rrb-group-d-2026-cbt-admit-card', 'Railway Recruitment Boards have released the RRB Group D Level-1 2026 CBT admit card. Candidates can download the e-call letter and city intimation slip from rrbcdg.gov.in and the regional RRB websites.', '<h2>RRB Group D 2026 CBT Admit Card – Download Hall Ticket</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Boards has released the <strong>admit card</strong> for the RRB Group D 2026 CBT Admit Card examination on its official website https://rrbcdg.gov.in. The admit card, also known as the call letter or hall ticket, is one of the most important documents that every candidate must carry to the examination centre, since no candidate is permitted to enter the examination hall without a valid printed admit card and a matching original photo identity proof. Candidates who successfully submitted their applications can now download their admit card by logging in with their credentials.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Railway Recruitment Boards as part of the selection process for the post of RRB Group D 2026 CBT Admit Card. Group D posts form the operational backbone of Indian Railways. The admit card contains essential information such as the candidate''''s name, roll number, registration number, photograph, signature, examination date, reporting time, shift, and the complete address of the allotted examination centre, along with detailed instructions that every candidate must read and follow carefully on the day of the examination.</p><h3>How to Download the Admit Card</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://rrbcdg.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the admit card or call letter download link for RRB Group D 2026 CBT Admit Card.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password as applicable.</li><li>The admit card will be displayed on the screen with all your examination details.</li><li>Verify the details, download the admit card and take a clear printout on A4 size paper.</li></ol><h3>Documents to Carry</h3><p>Candidates must carry the printed copy of the admit card along with at least one original valid photo identity proof such as Aadhaar Card, Voter ID, PAN Card, Driving Licence or Passport. A recent passport-size colour photograph identical to the one uploaded during the application must also be carried and affixed where required. Candidates who fail to bring these documents will not be allowed to appear in the examination under any circumstances.</p><h3>Important Instructions</h3><p>Candidates are advised to reach the examination centre well before the reporting time indicated on the admit card, as late entry is strictly prohibited. Biometric verification, frisking and document checks are carried out at the centre and may take considerable time. Electronic gadgets including mobile phones, calculators, smartwatches, Bluetooth devices, and any printed or written study material are strictly banned inside the examination hall. Candidates must carefully verify every detail printed on the admit card and immediately report any discrepancy to the conducting authority.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates who meet the prescribed qualification, namely a 10th class pass, or a National Apprenticeship Certificate, or an ITI certificate from an NCVT/SCVT recognized institution. Candidates who applied for the RRB Group D 2026 recruitment can download the CBT e-call letter after the release of the exam city intimation slip. The age criterion for the post is 18 to 36 years as on the cut-off date. Candidates appearing in the examination should ensure that they continue to satisfy all eligibility conditions, as these are verified during the document verification stage that follows the written examination.</p><h3>Selection Process & Next Steps</h3><p>The overall selection for this recruitment consists of a single Computer Based Test, a Physical Efficiency Test, document verification and a medical examination.  After appearing in the examination for which this admit card is issued, candidates should regularly monitor the official website https://rrbcdg.gov.in for the answer key, result and the schedule of subsequent stages. It is advisable to retain the admit card safely even after the examination, as it is often required at later stages such as document verification and counselling.</p>', 'Railways', 'RRB', 'Railway Recruitment Boards', 'admitcard', '2026-06-08', '2026-10-16', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-20', '2026-10-16', NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 32438, '18 to 36 years as on the cut-off date', 'a 10th class pass, or a National Apprenticeship Certificate, or an ITI certificate from an NCVT/SCVT recognized institution', 'Candidates who applied for the RRB Group D 2026 recruitment can download the CBT e-call letter after the release of the exam city intimation slip.', 500.00, 500.00, 250.00, 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in', 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in', 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in/group-d-2026-admit.pdf', 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in/admit-card', NULL, NULL, 'admitcard', 'ADMIT_CARD', 0, 1, 'RRB Group D 2026 CBT Admit Card – Download at rrbcdg.gov.in', 'RRB Group D 2026 CBT admit card and city slip released. Download e-call letter at rrbcdg.gov.in using registration number and date of birth.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
