(NULL, 'NEET PG 2026 Admit Card – Download NBEMS Hall Ticket', 'neet-pg-2026-admit-card', 'National Board of Examinations in Medical Sciences has released the NEET PG 2026 admit card. Candidates can download the hall ticket from natboard.edu.in using their application credentials for postgraduate medical admission.', '<h2>NEET PG 2026 Admit Card – Download NBEMS Hall Ticket</h2><p>The National Board of Examinations in Medical Sciences has released the <strong>admit card</strong> for the NEET PG 2026 Admit Card examination on its official website https://natboard.edu.in. The admit card, also known as the call letter or hall ticket, is one of the most important documents that every candidate must carry to the examination centre, since no candidate is permitted to enter the examination hall without a valid printed admit card and a matching original photo identity proof. Candidates who successfully submitted their applications can now download their admit card by logging in with their credentials.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the National Board of Examinations in Medical Sciences as part of the selection process for the post of NEET PG 2026 Admit Card. NEET PG is the qualifying examination for admission to MD, MS and PG Diploma courses across India. The admit card contains essential information such as the candidate''''s name, roll number, registration number, photograph, signature, examination date, reporting time, shift, and the complete address of the allotted examination centre, along with detailed instructions that every candidate must read and follow carefully on the day of the examination.</p><h3>How to Download the Admit Card</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://natboard.edu.in.</li><li>Click on the admit card or call letter download link for NEET PG 2026 Admit Card.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password as applicable.</li><li>The admit card will be displayed on the screen with all your examination details.</li><li>Verify the details, download the admit card and take a clear printout on A4 size paper.</li></ol><h3>Documents to Carry</h3><p>Candidates must carry the printed copy of the admit card along with at least one original valid photo identity proof such as Aadhaar Card, Voter ID, PAN Card, Driving Licence or Passport. A recent passport-size colour photograph identical to the one uploaded during the application must also be carried and affixed where required. Candidates who fail to bring these documents will not be allowed to appear in the examination under any circumstances.</p><h3>Important Instructions</h3><p>Candidates are advised to reach the examination centre well before the reporting time indicated on the admit card, as late entry is strictly prohibited. Biometric verification, frisking and document checks are carried out at the centre and may take considerable time. Electronic gadgets including mobile phones, calculators, smartwatches, Bluetooth devices, and any printed or written study material are strictly banned inside the examination hall. Candidates must carefully verify every detail printed on the admit card and immediately report any discrepancy to the conducting authority.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates who meet the prescribed qualification, namely an MBBS degree recognized as per the National Medical Commission Act along with a completed or provisional one-year internship from a recognized institution. Candidates must possess a permanent or provisional registration certificate and must have completed the prescribed internship by the cut-off date to download the admit card. The age criterion for the post is no upper age limit as prescribed by the conducting authority. Candidates appearing in the examination should ensure that they continue to satisfy all eligibility conditions, as these are verified during the document verification stage that follows the written examination.</p><h3>Selection Process & Next Steps</h3><p>The overall selection for this recruitment consists of a single computer based entrance examination, the score of which is used for counselling and admission to postgraduate medical courses.  After appearing in the examination for which this admit card is issued, candidates should regularly monitor the official website https://natboard.edu.in for the answer key, result and the schedule of subsequent stages. It is advisable to retain the admit card safely even after the examination, as it is often required at later stages such as document verification and counselling.</p>', 'Admission', 'NBEMS', 'National Board of Examinations in Medical Sciences', 'admitcard', '2026-03-15', '2026-06-10', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-15', '2026-06-10', NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', NULL, 'no upper age limit as prescribed by the conducting authority', 'an MBBS degree recognized as per the National Medical Commission Act along with a completed or provisional one-year internship from a recognized institution', 'Candidates must possess a permanent or provisional registration certificate and must have completed the prescribed internship by the cut-off date to download the admit card.', 3500.00, 3500.00, 2500.00, 'https://natboard.edu.in', 'https://natboard.edu.in', 'https://natboard.edu.in/neet-pg-2026-admit.pdf', 'https://natboard.edu.in', NULL, NULL, 'admitcard', 'ADMIT_CARD', 0, 1, 'NEET PG 2026 Admit Card – Download Hall Ticket at natboard.edu.in', 'NEET PG 2026 admit card released by NBEMS. Download hall ticket at natboard.edu.in using application credentials. Check exam date and instructions.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
