l your examination details.</li><li>Verify the details, download the admit card and take a clear printout on A4 size paper.</li></ol><h3>Documents to Carry</h3><p>Candidates must carry the printed copy of the admit card along with at least one original valid photo identity proof such as Aadhaar Card, Voter ID, PAN Card, Driving Licence or Passport. A recent passport-size colour photograph identical to the one uploaded during the application must also be carried and affixed where required. Candidates who fail to bring these documents will not be allowed to appear in the examination under any circumstances.</p><h3>Important Instructions</h3><p>Candidates are advised to reach the examination centre well before the reporting time indicated on the admit card, as late entry is strictly prohibited. Biometric verification, frisking and document checks are carried out at the centre and may take considerable time. Electronic gadgets including mobile phones, calculators, smartwatches, Bluetooth devices, and any printed or written study material are strictly banned inside the examination hall. Candidates must carefully verify every detail printed on the admit card and immediately report any discrepancy to the conducting authority.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates who meet the prescribed qualification, namely a pass in the 12th Standard (10+2) or equivalent examination with Physics, Chemistry and Mathematics, or candidates appearing in 12th in the current year, from a recognized Board. Candidates who registered for JEE Main 2026 Session 1 can download the admit card after the release of the advance city intimation slip. The age criterion for the post is no age limit, subject to the year of passing the qualifying examination as per eligibility norms. Candidates appearing in the examination should ensure that they continue to satisfy all eligibility conditions, as these are verified during the document verification stage that follows the written examination.</p><h3>Selection Process & Next Steps</h3><p>The overall selection for this recruitment consists of a computer based test (Paper 1 for B.E./B.Tech and Paper 2 for B.Arch/B.Planning), the score of which is used for admission and JEE Advanced eligibility.  After appearing in the examination for which this admit card is issued, candidates should regularly monitor the official website https://jeemain.nta.nic.in for the answer key, result and the schedule of subsequent stages. It is advisable to retain the admit card safely even after the examination, as it is often required at later stages such as document verification and counselling.</p>', 'Admission', 'NTA', 'National Testing Agency', 'admitcard', '2025-11-01', '2026-01-20', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-01-24', '2026-01-20', NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', NULL, 'no age limit, subject to the year of passing the qualifying examination as per eligibility norms', 'a pass in the 12th Standard (10+2) or equivalent examination with Physics, Chemistry and Mathematics, or candidates appearing in 12th in the current year, from a recognized Board', 'Candidates who registered for JEE Main 2026 Session 1 can download the admit card after the release of the advance city intimation slip.', 1000.00, 1000.00, 500.00, 'https://jeemain.nta.nic.in', 'https://jeemain.nta.nic.in', 'https://jeemain.nta.nic.in/session1-2026-admit.pdf', 'https://jeemain.nta.nic.in', NULL, NULL, 'admitcard', 'ADMIT_CARD', 0, 1, 'JEE Main 2026 Session 1 Admit Card – Download at NTA', 'JEE Main 2026 Session 1 admit card released. Download hall ticket at jeemain.nta.nic.in using application number and date of birth. Check exam city slip.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'CSIR UGC NET 2026 Admit Card – Download NTA Hall Ticket', 'csir-ugc-net-2026-admit-card', 'National Testing Agency has released the CSIR UGC NET 2026 admit card. Candidates can download the hall ticket from csirnet.nta.ac.in using their application number and date of birth for JRF and Assistant Professor eligibility.', '<h2>CSIR UGC NET 2026 Admit Card – Download NTA Hall Ticket</h2><p>The National Testing Agency has released the <strong>admit card</strong> for the CSIR UGC NET 2026 Admit Card examination on its official website https://csirnet.nta.ac.in. The admit card, also known as the call letter or hall ticket, is one of the most important documents that every candidate must carry to the examination centre, since no candidate is permitted to enter the examination hall without a valid printed admit card and a matching original photo identity proof. Candidates who successfully submitted their applications can now download their admit card by logging in with their credentials.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the National Testing Agency as part of the selection process for the post of CSIR UGC NET 2026 Admit Card. CSIR UGC NET is conducted for determining eligibility in science and technology streams. The admit card contains essential information such as the candidate''''s name, roll number, registration number, photograph, signature, examination date, reporting time, shift, and the complete address of the allotted examination centre, along with detailed instructions that every candidate must read and follow carefully on the day of the examination.</p><h3>How to Download the Admit Card</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://csirnet.nta.ac.in.</li><li>Click on the admit card or call letter download link for CSIR UGC NET 2026 Admit Card.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password as applicable.</li><li>The admit card will be displayed on the screen with all your examination details.</li><li>Verify the details, download the admit card and take a clear printout on A4 size paper.</li></ol><h3>Documents to Carry</h3><p>Candidates must carry the printed copy of the admit card along with at least one original valid photo identity proof such as Aadhaar Card, Voter ID, PAN Card, Driving Licence or Passport. A recent passport-size colour photograph identical to the one uploaded during the application must also be carried and affixed where required. Candidates who fail to bring these documents will not be allowed to appear in the examination under any circumstances.</p><h3>Important Instructions</h3><p>Candidates are advised to reach the examination centre well before the reporting time indicated on the admit card, as late entry is strictly prohibited. Biometric verification, frisking and document checks are carried out at the centre and may take considerable time. Electronic gadgets including mobile phones, calculators, smartwatches, Bluetooth devices, and any printed or written study material are strictly banned inside the examination hall. Candidates must carefully verify every detail printed on the admit card and immediately report any discrepancy to the conducting authority.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates who meet the prescribed qualification, namely a Master''''s Degree or equivalent in Science subjects with the prescribed minimum percentage of marks from a recognized University. Candidates who registered for the CSIR UGC NET 2026 in science streams such as Chemical, Earth, Life, Mathematical and Physical Sciences can download the admit card. The age criterion for the post is below 30 years for JRF (with relaxation) and no upper age limit for Assistant Professor and Lectureship. Candidates appearing in the examination should ensure that they continue to satisfy all eligibility conditions, as these are verified during the document verification stage that follows the written examination.</p><h3>Selection Process & Next Steps</h3><p>The overall selection for this recruitment consists of a single computer based test divided into three parts, the score determining eligibility for JRF, Lectureship and PhD admission.  After appearing in the examination for which this admit card is issued, candidates should regularly monitor the official website https://csirnet.nta.ac.in for the answer key, result and the schedule of subsequent stages. It is advisable to retain the admit card safely even after the examination, as it is often required at later stages such as document verification and counselling.</p>', 'Teaching', 'NTA', 'National Testing Agency', 'admitcard', '2026-04-10', '2026-06-14', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-20', '2026-06-14', NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', NULL, 'below 30 years for JRF (with relaxation) and no upper age limit for Assistant Professor and Lectureship', 'a Master''''s Degree or equivalent in Science subjects with the prescribed minimum percentage of marks from a recognized University', 'Candidates who registered for the CSIR UGC NET 2026 in science streams such as Chemical, Earth, Life, Mathematical and Physical Sciences can download the admit card.', 1150.00, 600.00, 325.00, 'https://csirnet.nta.ac.in', 'https://csirnet.nta.ac.in', 'https://csirnet.nta.ac.in/2026-admit.pdf', 'https://csirnet.nta.ac.in', NULL, NULL, 'admitcard', 'ADMIT_CARD', 0, 1, 'CSIR UGC NET 2026 Admit Card – Download Hall Ticket at NTA', 'CSIR UGC NET 2026 admit card released. Download hall ticket at csirnet.nta.ac.in using application number and date of birth. Check exam pattern.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'RRB Technician 2026 CBT Admit Card – Download e-Call Letter', 'rrb-technician-2026-cbt-admit-card', 'Railway Recruitment Boards have released the RRB Technician 2026 CBT admit card and city intimation slip. Candidates can download the e-call letter from rrbcdg.gov.in and the regional RRB websites.', '<h2>RRB Technician 2026 CBT Admit Card – Download e-Call Letter</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Boards has released the <strong>admit card</strong> for the RRB Technician 2026 CBT Admit Card examination on its official website https://rrbcdg.gov.in. The admit card, also known as the call letter or hall ticket, is one of the most important documents that every candidate must carry to the examination centre, since no candidate is permitted to enter the examination hall without a valid printed admit card and a matching original photo identity proof. Candidates who successfully submitted their applications can now download their admit card by logging in with their credentials.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Railway Recruitment Boards as part of the selection process for the post of RRB Technician 2026 CBT Admit Card. The Technician post is a key technical role across various railway departments. The admit card contains essential information such as the candidate''''s name, roll number, registration number, photograph, signature, examination date, reporting time, shift, and the complete address of the allotted examination centre, along with detailed instructions that every candidate must read and follow carefully on the day of the examination.</p><h3>How to Download the Admit Card</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://rrbcdg.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the admit card or call letter download link for RRB Technician 2026 CBT Admit Card.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password as applicable.</li><li>The admit card will be displayed on the screen with all your examination details.</li><li>Verify the details, download the admit card and take a clear printout on A4 size paper.</li></ol><h3>Documents to Carry</h3><p>Candidates must carry the printed copy of the admit card along with at least one original valid photo identity proof such as Aadhaar Card, Voter ID, PAN Card, Driving Licence or Passport. A recent passport-size colour photograph identical to the one uploaded during the application must also be carried and affixed where required. Candidates who fail to bring these documents will not be allowed to appear in the examination under any circumstances.</p><h3>Important Instructions</h3><p>Candidates are advised to reach the examination centre well before the reporting time indicated on the admit card, as late entry is strictly prohibited. Biometric verification, frisking and document checks are carried out at the centre and may take considerable time. Electronic gadgets including mobile phones, calculators, smartwatches, Bluetooth devices, and any printed or written study material are strictly banned inside the examination hall. Candidates must carefully verify every detail printed on the admit card and immediately report any discrepancy to the conducting authority.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates who meet the prescribed qualification, namely a 10th class pass with ITI in the relevant trade from NCVT/SCVT for Technician Grade III, and a Diploma or Degree in the relevant engineering branch for Technician Grade I posts. Candidates who applied for the RRB Technician 2026 recruitment can download the CBT e-call letter after the exam city intimation slip is released. The age criterion for the post is 18 to 33 years as on the cut-off date. Candidates appearing in the examination should ensure that they continue to satisfy all eligibility conditions, as these are verified during the document verification stage that follows the written examination.</p><h3>Selection Process & Next Steps</h3><p>The overall selection for this recruitment consists of a Computer Based Test, document verification and a medical examination.  After appearing in the examination for which this admit card is issued, candidates should regularly monitor the official website https://rrbcdg.gov.in for the answer key, result and the schedule of subsequent stages. It is advisable to retain the admit card safely even after the examination, as it is often required at later stages such as document verification and counselling.</p>', 'Railways', 'RRB', 'Railway Recruitment Boards', 'admitcard', '2026-04-20', '2026-06-13', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-18', '2026-06-13', NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 14298, '18 to 33 years as on the cut-off date', 'a 10th class pass with ITI in the relevant trade from NCVT/SCVT for Technician Grade III, and a Diploma or Degree in the relevant engineering branch for Technician Grade I posts', 'Candidates who applied for the RRB Technician 2026 recruitment can download the CBT e-call letter after the exam city intimation slip is released.', 500.00, 500.00, 250.00, 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in', 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in', 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in/technician-2026-admit.pdf', 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in/admit-card', NULL, NULL, 'admitcard', 'ADMIT_CARD', 0, 1, 'RRB Technician 2026 CBT Admit Card – Download at rrbcdg.gov.in', 'RRB Technician 2026 CBT admit card and city slip released. Download e-call letter at rrbcdg.gov.in using registration number and date of birth.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
