fy the details, download the admit card and take a clear printout on A4 size paper.</li></ol><h3>Documents to Carry</h3><p>Candidates must carry the printed copy of the admit card along with at least one original valid photo identity proof such as Aadhaar Card, Voter ID, PAN Card, Driving Licence or Passport. A recent passport-size colour photograph identical to the one uploaded during the application must also be carried and affixed where required. Candidates who fail to bring these documents will not be allowed to appear in the examination under any circumstances.</p><h3>Important Instructions</h3><p>Candidates are advised to reach the examination centre well before the reporting time indicated on the admit card, as late entry is strictly prohibited. Biometric verification, frisking and document checks are carried out at the centre and may take considerable time. Electronic gadgets including mobile phones, calculators, smartwatches, Bluetooth devices, and any printed or written study material are strictly banned inside the examination hall. Candidates must carefully verify every detail printed on the admit card and immediately report any discrepancy to the conducting authority.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates who meet the prescribed qualification, namely a pass in the 10th class (Matriculation) examination from a recognized Board. Candidates who applied for the RPF Constable recruitment can download the Computer Based Test admit card after the city intimation slip is released. The age criterion for the post is 18 to 28 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories. Candidates appearing in the examination should ensure that they continue to satisfy all eligibility conditions, as these are verified during the document verification stage that follows the written examination.</p><h3>Selection Process & Next Steps</h3><p>The overall selection for this recruitment consists of a Computer Based Test, a Physical Efficiency Test, a Physical Measurement Test and document verification.  After appearing in the examination for which this admit card is issued, candidates should regularly monitor the official website https://rrbcdg.gov.in for the answer key, result and the schedule of subsequent stages. It is advisable to retain the admit card safely even after the examination, as it is often required at later stages such as document verification and counselling.</p>', 'Railways', 'RRB', 'Railway Protection Force', 'admitcard', '2026-04-10', '2026-06-11', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19', '2026-06-11', NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 4660, '18 to 28 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories', 'a pass in the 10th class (Matriculation) examination from a recognized Board', 'Candidates who applied for the RPF Constable recruitment can download the Computer Based Test admit card after the city intimation slip is released.', 500.00, 500.00, 250.00, 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in', 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in', 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in/rpf-constable-2026-admit.pdf', 'https://rrbcdg.gov.in/admit-card', NULL, NULL, 'admitcard', 'ADMIT_CARD', 0, 1, 'RPF Constable 2026 Admit Card – Download CBT Hall Ticket', 'RPF Constable 2026 CBT admit card released. Download hall ticket at rrbcdg.gov.in using registration number and date of birth. Check exam details.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'MPPSC State Service Prelims 2026 Admit Card – Download Online', 'mppsc-state-service-prelims-2026-admit-card', 'Madhya Pradesh Public Service Commission has released the State Service Preliminary Examination 2026 admit card. Candidates can download the admit card from mppsc.mp.gov.in using their application number and date of birth.', '<h2>MPPSC State Service Prelims 2026 Admit Card – Download Online</h2><p>The Madhya Pradesh Public Service Commission has released the <strong>admit card</strong> for the MPPSC State Service Prelims 2026 Admit Card examination on its official website https://mppsc.mp.gov.in. The admit card, also known as the call letter or hall ticket, is one of the most important documents that every candidate must carry to the examination centre, since no candidate is permitted to enter the examination hall without a valid printed admit card and a matching original photo identity proof. Candidates who successfully submitted their applications can now download their admit card by logging in with their credentials.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Madhya Pradesh Public Service Commission as part of the selection process for the post of MPPSC State Service Prelims 2026 Admit Card. The State Service Examination recruits for administrative and allied posts in the Madhya Pradesh Government. The admit card contains essential information such as the candidate''''s name, roll number, registration number, photograph, signature, examination date, reporting time, shift, and the complete address of the allotted examination centre, along with detailed instructions that every candidate must read and follow carefully on the day of the examination.</p><h3>How to Download the Admit Card</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://mppsc.mp.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the admit card or call letter download link for MPPSC State Service Prelims 2026 Admit Card.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password as applicable.</li><li>The admit card will be displayed on the screen with all your examination details.</li><li>Verify the details, download the admit card and take a clear printout on A4 size paper.</li></ol><h3>Documents to Carry</h3><p>Candidates must carry the printed copy of the admit card along with at least one original valid photo identity proof such as Aadhaar Card, Voter ID, PAN Card, Driving Licence or Passport. A recent passport-size colour photograph identical to the one uploaded during the application must also be carried and affixed where required. Candidates who fail to bring these documents will not be allowed to appear in the examination under any circumstances.</p><h3>Important Instructions</h3><p>Candidates are advised to reach the examination centre well before the reporting time indicated on the admit card, as late entry is strictly prohibited. Biometric verification, frisking and document checks are carried out at the centre and may take considerable time. Electronic gadgets including mobile phones, calculators, smartwatches, Bluetooth devices, and any printed or written study material are strictly banned inside the examination hall. Candidates must carefully verify every detail printed on the admit card and immediately report any discrepancy to the conducting authority.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates who meet the prescribed qualification, namely a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline from a recognized University or an equivalent qualification. Candidates who applied for the MPPSC State Service Examination can download the preliminary examination admit card from the official commission website. The age criterion for the post is 21 to 40 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories of Madhya Pradesh. Candidates appearing in the examination should ensure that they continue to satisfy all eligibility conditions, as these are verified during the document verification stage that follows the written examination.</p><h3>Selection Process & Next Steps</h3><p>The overall selection for this recruitment consists of a preliminary examination, a main examination and an interview.  After appearing in the examination for which this admit card is issued, candidates should regularly monitor the official website https://mppsc.mp.gov.in for the answer key, result and the schedule of subsequent stages. It is advisable to retain the admit card safely even after the examination, as it is often required at later stages such as document verification and counselling.</p>', 'State Govt', 'MPPSC', 'Madhya Pradesh Public Service Commission', 'admitcard', '2026-03-01', '2026-06-12', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-21', '2026-06-12', NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 158, '21 to 40 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation for reserved categories of Madhya Pradesh', 'a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline from a recognized University or an equivalent qualification', 'Candidates who applied for the MPPSC State Service Examination can download the preliminary examination admit card from the official commission website.', 250.00, 250.00, 250.00, 'https://mppsc.mp.gov.in', 'https://mppsc.mp.gov.in', 'https://mppsc.mp.gov.in/state-service-prelims-2026-admit.pdf', 'https://mppsc.mp.gov.in', NULL, NULL, 'admitcard', 'ADMIT_CARD', 0, 1, 'MPPSC State Service Prelims 2026 Admit Card – Download Online', 'MPPSC State Service Preliminary 2026 admit card released. Download at mppsc.mp.gov.in using application number and date of birth. Check exam pattern.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'SSC CGL 2026 Tier-I Result – Check Marks & Tier-II Shortlist', 'ssc-cgl-2026-tier-1-result', 'Staff Selection Commission has declared the SSC CGL 2026 Tier-I result. Candidates can check their qualifying status, marks and category-wise cut off at ssc.gov.in to proceed to the Tier-II examination.', '<h2>SSC CGL 2026 Tier-I Result – Check Marks & Tier-II Shortlist</h2><p>The Staff Selection Commission has declared the <strong>result</strong> of the SSC CGL 2026 Tier-I Result examination on its official website https://ssc.gov.in. Candidates who appeared in the examination can now check their qualifying status, marks and the category-wise cut off by logging in to the candidate portal or by checking the list of selected roll numbers published in the result notice. This result determines the candidates who are eligible to proceed to the next stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>About the Recruitment</h3><p>This recruitment is conducted by the Staff Selection Commission for the post of SSC CGL 2026 Tier-I Result. SSC CGL recruits for Group B and Group C posts in various central government ministries and departments. The result is processed on the basis of the marks obtained by the candidates, after applying normalisation where the examination is held in multiple shifts, and the category-wise cut off marks determined by the conducting authority based on the number of vacancies, the number of candidates and the overall difficulty of the examination.</p><h3>How to Check the Result</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://ssc.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the result link for the SSC CGL 2026 Tier-I Result examination.</li><li>A PDF containing the roll numbers of qualified or selected candidates will open.</li><li>Search for your roll number using the find option.</li><li>Log in with your registration number and date of birth to view your individual scorecard with detailed marks.</li></ol><h3>Cut Off Marks & Scorecard</h3><p>The cut off marks are released separately for each category, namely Unreserved, EWS, OBC, SC, ST and other applicable sub-categories. The individual scorecard displays the candidate''''s name, roll number, category, sectional and total marks, normalised marks where applicable, and the final qualifying status. Candidates are advised to download and preserve their scorecard, as it serves as an important record and may be required at later stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Next Steps for Qualified Candidates</h3><p>Candidates who have qualified must prepare for the subsequent stages of the selection process. The overall recruitment consists of a Tier-I Computer Based Examination, a Tier-II Computer Based Examination, document verification and a medical examination where applicable.  Qualified candidates should keep their educational certificates, category certificate, identity proof and recent photographs ready for document verification, and should regularly check the official website for the schedule of the next stage. The final merit and appointment are subject to successful completion of all remaining stages.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This recruitment is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline from a recognized University or equivalent. Candidates who qualify the Tier-I examination as per the category-wise cut off are shortlisted to appear in the Tier-II examination. The prescribed age limit is 18 to 32 years depending on the post. Candidates should note that meeting the eligibility conditions is mandatory and will be strictly verified before final selection.</p><h3>Important Note</h3><p>Candidates should rely solely on the official website https://ssc.gov.in for authentic result-related information and must beware of fraudulent agents or unofficial websites that claim to influence results. Any grievance regarding the result should be addressed to the Staff Selection Commission through the prescribed official channel within the timeframe specified in the result notice, after which representations are generally not entertained.</p>', 'Central Govt', 'SSC', 'Staff Selection Commission', 'result', '2026-05-21', '2026-10-05', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-15', NULL, '2026-10-05', '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 12256, '18 to 32 years depending on the post', 'a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline from a recognized University or equivalent', 'Candidates who qualify the Tier-I examination as per the category-wise cut off are shortlisted to appear in the Tier-II examination.', 100.00, 100.00, 0.00, 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in/cgl-2026-tier1-result.pdf', 'https://ssc.gov.in/result', NULL, NULL, 'result', 'RESULT', 1, 1, 'SSC CGL 2026 Tier-I Result – Check Marks & Cut Off at ssc.gov.in', 'SSC CGL 2026 Tier-I result declared. Check marks, category-wise cut off and Tier-II shortlist at ssc.gov.in using login credentials.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'SSC MTS 2026 Result – Check Final Merit & Cut Off Marks', 'ssc-mts-2026-result', 'Staff Selection Commission has declared the SSC MTS and Havaldar 2026 result. Candidates can check their marks and category-wise cut off at ssc.gov.in.', '<h2>SSC MTS 2026 Result – Check Final Merit & Cut Off Marks</h2><p>The Staff Selection Commission has declared the <strong>result</strong> of the SSC MTS 2026 Result examination on its official website https://ssc.gov.in. Candidates who appeared in the examination can now check their qualifying status, marks and the category-wise cut off by logging in to the candidate portal or by checking the list of selected roll numbers published in the result notice. This result determines the candidates who are eligible to proceed to the next stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>About the Recruitment</h3><p>This recruitment is conducted by the Staff Selection Commission for the post of SSC MTS 2026 Result. SSC MTS recruits Multi Tasking Staff and Havaldars for central government offices. The result is processed on the basis of the marks obtained by the candidates, after applying normalisation where the examination is held in multiple shifts, and the category-wise cut off marks determined by the conducting authority based on the number of vacancies, the number of candidates and the overall difficulty of the examination.</p><h3>How to Check the Result</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://ssc.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the result link for the SSC MTS 2026 Result examination.</li><li>A PDF containing the roll numbers of qualified or selected candidates will open.</li><li>Search for your roll number using the find option.</li><li>Log in with your registration number and date of birth to view your individual scorecard with detailed marks.</li></ol><h3>Cut Off Marks & Scorecard</h3><p>The cut off marks are released separately for each category, namely Unreserved, EWS, OBC, SC, ST and other applicable sub-categories. The individual scorecard displays the candidate''''s name, roll number, category, sectional and total marks, normalised marks where applicable, and the final qualifying status. Candidates are advised to download and preserve their scorecard, as it serves as an important record and may be required at later stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Next Steps for Qualified Candidates</h3><p>Candidates who have qualified must prepare for the subsequent stages of the selection process. The overall recruitment consists of a Computer Based Examination, and for Havaldar posts a Physical Efficiency Test and Physical Standard Test, followed by document verification.  Qualified candidates should keep their educational certificates, category certificate, identity proof and recent photographs ready for document verification, and should regularly check the official website for the schedule of the next stage. The final merit and appointment are subject to successful completion of all remaining stages.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This recruitment is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a pass in the 10th class (Matriculation) from a recognized Board. Candidates who qualify the Computer Based Examination as per the cut off are shortlisted, and Havaldar applicants additionally undergo a physical efficiency and standard test. The prescribed age limit is 18 to 25 years, with 18 to 27 years for some posts. Candidates should note that meeting the eligibility conditions is mandatory and will be strictly verified before final selection.</p><h3>Important Note</h3><p>Candidates should rely solely on the official website https://ssc.gov.in for authentic result-related information and must beware of fraudulent agents or unofficial websites that claim to influence results. Any grievance regarding the result should be addressed to the Staff Selection Commission through the prescribed official channel within the timeframe specified in the result notice, after which representations are generally not entertained.</p>', 'Central Govt', 'SSC', 'Staff Selection Commission', 'result', '2026-04-10', '2026-09-15', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-25', NULL, '2026-09-15', '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 8000, '18 to 25 years, with 18 to 27 years for some posts', 'a pass in the 10th class (Matriculation) from a recognized Board', 'Candidates who qualify the Computer Based Examination as per the cut off are shortlisted, and Havaldar applicants additionally undergo a physical efficiency and standard test.', 100.00, 100.00, 0.00, 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in/mts-2026-result.pdf', 'https://ssc.gov.in/result', NULL, NULL, 'result', 'RESULT', 0, 1, 'SSC MTS 2026 Result – Check Cut Off & Merit at ssc.gov.in', 'SSC MTS and Havaldar 2026 result declared. Check marks, category-wise cut off and PET/PST schedule at ssc.gov.in using login credentials.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'IBPS PO 2026 Prelims Result – Check Scorecard & Cut Off', 'ibps-po-2026-prelims-result', 'Institute of Banking Personnel Selection has declared the IBPS PO/MT XVI 2026 preliminary result. Candidates can check their qualifying status at ibps.in to proceed to the main examination.', '<h2>IBPS PO 2026 Prelims Result – Check Scorecard & Cut Off</h2><p>The Institute of Banking Personnel Selection has declared the <strong>result</strong> of the IBPS PO 2026 Prelims Result examination on its official website https://ibps.in. Candidates who appeared in the examination can now check their qualifying status, marks and the category-wise cut off by logging in to the candidate portal or by checking the list of selected roll numbers published in the result notice. This result determines the candidates who are eligible to proceed to the next stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>About the Recruitment</h3><p>This recruitment is conducted by the Institute of Banking Personnel Selection for the post of IBPS PO 2026 Prelims Result. IBPS PO recruits Probationary Officers for participating public sector banks. The result is processed on the basis of the marks obtained by the candidates, after applying normalisation where the examination is held in multiple shifts, and the category-wise cut off marks determined by the conducting authority based on the number of vacancies, the number of candidates and the overall difficulty of the examination.</p><h3>How to Check the Result</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://ibps.in.</li><li>Click on the result link for the IBPS PO 2026 Prelims Result examination.</li><li>A PDF containing the roll numbers of qualified or selected candidates will open.</li><li>Search for your roll number using the find option.</li><li>Log in with your registration number and date of birth to view your individual scorecard with detailed marks.</li></ol><h3>Cut Off Marks & Scorecard</h3><p>The cut off marks are released separately for each category, namely Unreserved, EWS, OBC, SC, ST and other applicable sub-categories. The individual scorecard displays the candidate''''s name, roll number, category, sectional and total marks, normalised marks where applicable, and the final qualifying status. Candidates are advised to download and preserve their scorecard, as it serves as an important record and may be required at later stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Next Steps for Qualified Candidates</h3><p>Candidates who have qualified must prepare for the subsequent stages of the selection process. The overall recruitment consists of a preliminary examination, a main examination and an interview, with the final merit based on the main examination and interview.  Qualified candidates should keep their educational certificates, category certificate, identity proof and recent photographs ready for document verification, and should regularly check the official website for the schedule of the next stage. The final merit and appointment are subject to successful completion of all remaining stages.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This recruitment is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a graduation degree in any discipline from a recognized University with basic computer knowledge. Candidates who qualify the preliminary examination as per the cut off are eligible to appear in the main examination, which decides the final merit. The prescribed age limit is 20 to 30 years as on the cut-off date. Candidates should note that meeting the eligibility conditions is mandatory and will be strictly verified before final selection.</p><h3>Important Note</h3><p>Candidates should rely solely on the official website https://ibps.in for authentic result-related information and must beware of fraudulent agents or unofficial websites that claim to influence results. Any grievance regarding the result should be addressed to the Institute of Banking Personnel Selection through the prescribed official channel within the timeframe specified in the result notice, after which representations are generally not entertained.</p>', 'Bank', 'IBPS', 'Institute of Banking Personnel Selection', 'result', '2026-06-10', '2026-09-10', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-22', NULL, '2026-09-10', '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 5208, '20 to 30 years as on the cut-off date', 'a graduation degree in any discipline from a recognized University with basic computer knowledge', 'Candidates who qualify the preliminary examination as per the cut off are eligible to appear in the main examination, which decides the final merit.', 850.00, 850.00, 175.00, 'https://ibps.in', 'https://ibps.in', 'https://ibps.in/po-xvi-prelims-result.pdf', 'https://ibps.in/result', NULL, NULL, 'result', 'RESULT', 0, 1, 'IBPS PO 2026 Prelims Result – Check Scorecard at ibps.in', 'IBPS PO/MT XVI 2026 preliminary result declared. Check qualifying status and cut off at ibps.in. Qualified candidates appear in the main examination.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
