(NULL, 'UPSC NDA & NA (I) 2026 Result – Check Written Exam Result', 'upsc-nda-na-i-2026-result', 'UPSC has declared the National Defence Academy and Naval Academy Examination (I) 2026 written result. Candidates can check the list of qualified roll numbers at upsc.gov.in for the SSB interview.', '<h2>UPSC NDA & NA (I) 2026 Result – Check Written Exam Result</h2><p>The Union Public Service Commission has declared the <strong>result</strong> of the UPSC NDA & NA (I) 2026 Result examination on its official website https://upsc.gov.in. Candidates who appeared in the examination can now check their qualifying status, marks and the category-wise cut off by logging in to the candidate portal or by checking the list of selected roll numbers published in the result notice. This result determines the candidates who are eligible to proceed to the next stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>About the Recruitment</h3><p>This recruitment is conducted by the Union Public Service Commission for the post of UPSC NDA & NA (I) 2026 Result. The NDA examination is the gateway to officer training in the National Defence Academy. The result is processed on the basis of the marks obtained by the candidates, after applying normalisation where the examination is held in multiple shifts, and the category-wise cut off marks determined by the conducting authority based on the number of vacancies, the number of candidates and the overall difficulty of the examination.</p><h3>How to Check the Result</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://upsc.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the result link for the UPSC NDA & NA (I) 2026 Result examination.</li><li>A PDF containing the roll numbers of qualified or selected candidates will open.</li><li>Search for your roll number using the find option.</li><li>Log in with your registration number and date of birth to view your individual scorecard with detailed marks.</li></ol><h3>Cut Off Marks & Scorecard</h3><p>The cut off marks are released separately for each category, namely Unreserved, EWS, OBC, SC, ST and other applicable sub-categories. The individual scorecard displays the candidate''''s name, roll number, category, sectional and total marks, normalised marks where applicable, and the final qualifying status. Candidates are advised to download and preserve their scorecard, as it serves as an important record and may be required at later stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Next Steps for Qualified Candidates</h3><p>Candidates who have qualified must prepare for the subsequent stages of the selection process. The overall recruitment consists of a written examination conducted by UPSC, followed by an SSB interview and a medical examination.  Qualified candidates should keep their educational certificates, category certificate, identity proof and recent photographs ready for document verification, and should regularly check the official website for the schedule of the next stage. The final merit and appointment are subject to successful completion of all remaining stages.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This recruitment is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a pass in the 12th class for the Army wing, and 12th with Physics and Mathematics for the Air Force, Navy and Naval Academy wings, from a recognized Board. Candidates who qualify the written examination are called for the Services Selection Board (SSB) interview and personality test. The prescribed age limit is approximately 16.5 to 19.5 years, for unmarried male and female candidates. Candidates should note that meeting the eligibility conditions is mandatory and will be strictly verified before final selection.</p><h3>Important Note</h3><p>Candidates should rely solely on the official website https://upsc.gov.in for authentic result-related information and must beware of fraudulent agents or unofficial websites that claim to influence results. Any grievance regarding the result should be addressed to the Union Public Service Commission through the prescribed official channel within the timeframe specified in the result notice, after which representations are generally not entertained.</p>', 'Defence', 'UPSC', 'Union Public Service Commission', 'result', '2025-12-11', '2026-06-05', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-13', NULL, '2026-06-05', '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 406, 'approximately 16.5 to 19.5 years, for unmarried male and female candidates', 'a pass in the 12th class for the Army wing, and 12th with Physics and Mathematics for the Air Force, Navy and Naval Academy wings, from a recognized Board', 'Candidates who qualify the written examination are called for the Services Selection Board (SSB) interview and personality test.', 100.00, 100.00, 0.00, 'https://upsc.gov.in', 'https://upsc.gov.in', 'https://upsc.gov.in/NDA-I-2026-Result.pdf', 'https://upsc.gov.in/examinations/results', NULL, NULL, 'result', 'RESULT', 0, 1, 'UPSC NDA 1 2026 Result – Check Written Exam Result at upsc.gov.in', 'UPSC NDA & NA (I) 2026 written result declared. Check qualified roll numbers at upsc.gov.in for the SSB interview. Exam held on 13 April 2026.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
