(NULL, 'UP Police Constable 2026 Result – Check Merit & Cut Off', 'up-police-constable-2026-result', 'Uttar Pradesh Police Recruitment and Promotion Board has declared the UP Police Constable 2026 written examination result. Candidates can check their marks and category-wise cut off at uppbpb.gov.in.', '<h2>UP Police Constable 2026 Result – Check Merit & Cut Off</h2><p>The Uttar Pradesh Police Recruitment and Promotion Board has declared the <strong>result</strong> of the UP Police Constable 2026 Result examination on its official website https://uppbpb.gov.in. Candidates who appeared in the examination can now check their qualifying status, marks and the category-wise cut off by logging in to the candidate portal or by checking the list of selected roll numbers published in the result notice. This result determines the candidates who are eligible to proceed to the next stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>About the Recruitment</h3><p>This recruitment is conducted by the Uttar Pradesh Police Recruitment and Promotion Board for the post of UP Police Constable 2026 Result. The Constable post offers a stable career in the Uttar Pradesh Police. The result is processed on the basis of the marks obtained by the candidates, after applying normalisation where the examination is held in multiple shifts, and the category-wise cut off marks determined by the conducting authority based on the number of vacancies, the number of candidates and the overall difficulty of the examination.</p><h3>How to Check the Result</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://uppbpb.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the result link for the UP Police Constable 2026 Result examination.</li><li>A PDF containing the roll numbers of qualified or selected candidates will open.</li><li>Search for your roll number using the find option.</li><li>Log in with your registration number and date of birth to view your individual scorecard with detailed marks.</li></ol><h3>Cut Off Marks & Scorecard</h3><p>The cut off marks are released separately for each category, namely Unreserved, EWS, OBC, SC, ST and other applicable sub-categories. The individual scorecard displays the candidate''''s name, roll number, category, sectional and total marks, normalised marks where applicable, and the final qualifying status. Candidates are advised to download and preserve their scorecard, as it serves as an important record and may be required at later stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Next Steps for Qualified Candidates</h3><p>Candidates who have qualified must prepare for the subsequent stages of the selection process. The overall recruitment consists of a written examination, document verification, a physical standard test and a physical efficiency test.  Qualified candidates should keep their educational certificates, category certificate, identity proof and recent photographs ready for document verification, and should regularly check the official website for the schedule of the next stage. The final merit and appointment are subject to successful completion of all remaining stages.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This recruitment is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a pass in the Intermediate (12th) examination from a Board recognized by the Government of Uttar Pradesh, with UP domicile. Candidates who qualify the written examination are shortlisted for document verification, the physical standard test and the physical efficiency test. The prescribed age limit is 18 to 22 years for male and 18 to 25 years for female candidates. Candidates should note that meeting the eligibility conditions is mandatory and will be strictly verified before final selection.</p><h3>Important Note</h3><p>Candidates should rely solely on the official website https://uppbpb.gov.in for authentic result-related information and must beware of fraudulent agents or unofficial websites that claim to influence results. Any grievance regarding the result should be addressed to the Uttar Pradesh Police Recruitment and Promotion Board through the prescribed official channel within the timeframe specified in the result notice, after which representations are generally not entertained.</p>', 'State Govt', 'UPPRPB', 'Uttar Pradesh Police Recruitment and Promotion Board', 'result', '2026-05-25', '2026-11-20', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-15', NULL, '2026-11-20', '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 19220, '18 to 22 years for male and 18 to 25 years for female candidates', 'a pass in the Intermediate (12th) examination from a Board recognized by the Government of Uttar Pradesh, with UP domicile', 'Candidates who qualify the written examination are shortlisted for document verification, the physical standard test and the physical efficiency test.', 400.00, 400.00, 400.00, 'https://uppbpb.gov.in', 'https://uppbpb.gov.in', 'https://uppbpb.gov.in/constable-2026-result.pdf', 'https://uppbpb.gov.in/result', NULL, NULL, 'result', 'RESULT', 0, 1, 'UP Police Constable 2026 Result – Check Merit at uppbpb.gov.in', 'UP Police Constable 2026 written exam result declared. Check marks, category-wise cut off and PST/PET schedule at uppbpb.gov.in.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
