(NULL, 'JEE Main 2026 Session 1 Result – Check Percentile & NTA Score', 'jee-main-2026-session-1-result', 'National Testing Agency has declared the JEE Main 2026 Session 1 result. Candidates can check their NTA percentile score at jeemain.nta.nic.in for engineering admissions and JEE Advanced eligibility.', '<h2>JEE Main 2026 Session 1 Result – Check Percentile & NTA Score</h2><p>The National Testing Agency has declared the <strong>result</strong> of the JEE Main 2026 Session 1 Result examination on its official website https://jeemain.nta.nic.in. Candidates who appeared in the examination can now check their qualifying status, marks and the category-wise cut off by logging in to the candidate portal or by checking the list of selected roll numbers published in the result notice. This result determines the candidates who are eligible to proceed to the next stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>About the Recruitment</h3><p>This recruitment is conducted by the National Testing Agency for the post of JEE Main 2026 Session 1 Result. JEE Main is the gateway to premier engineering institutions in the country. The result is processed on the basis of the marks obtained by the candidates, after applying normalisation where the examination is held in multiple shifts, and the category-wise cut off marks determined by the conducting authority based on the number of vacancies, the number of candidates and the overall difficulty of the examination.</p><h3>How to Check the Result</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://jeemain.nta.nic.in.</li><li>Click on the result link for the JEE Main 2026 Session 1 Result examination.</li><li>A PDF containing the roll numbers of qualified or selected candidates will open.</li><li>Search for your roll number using the find option.</li><li>Log in with your registration number and date of birth to view your individual scorecard with detailed marks.</li></ol><h3>Cut Off Marks & Scorecard</h3><p>The cut off marks are released separately for each category, namely Unreserved, EWS, OBC, SC, ST and other applicable sub-categories. The individual scorecard displays the candidate''''s name, roll number, category, sectional and total marks, normalised marks where applicable, and the final qualifying status. Candidates are advised to download and preserve their scorecard, as it serves as an important record and may be required at later stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Next Steps for Qualified Candidates</h3><p>Candidates who have qualified must prepare for the subsequent stages of the selection process. The overall recruitment consists of a computer based test, the percentile score of which is used for admission to NITs, IIITs and CFTIs and for JEE Advanced eligibility.  Qualified candidates should keep their educational certificates, category certificate, identity proof and recent photographs ready for document verification, and should regularly check the official website for the schedule of the next stage. The final merit and appointment are subject to successful completion of all remaining stages.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This recruitment is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a pass in the 12th Standard (10+2) with Physics, Chemistry and Mathematics, or candidates appearing in 12th in the current year, from a recognized Board. Candidates who appeared in Session 1 can check their percentile score, which is normalised across multiple shifts and used for admission and merit. The prescribed age limit is no age limit, subject to the year of passing the qualifying examination. Candidates should note that meeting the eligibility conditions is mandatory and will be strictly verified before final selection.</p><h3>Important Note</h3><p>Candidates should rely solely on the official website https://jeemain.nta.nic.in for authentic result-related information and must beware of fraudulent agents or unofficial websites that claim to influence results. Any grievance regarding the result should b