EWS, OBC, SC, ST and other applicable sub-categories. The individual scorecard displays the candidate''''s name, roll number, category, sectional and total marks, normalised marks where applicable, and the final qualifying status. Candidates are advised to download and preserve their scorecard, as it serves as an important record and may be required at later stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Next Steps for Qualified Candidates</h3><p>Candidates who have qualified must prepare for the subsequent stages of the selection process. The overall recruitment consists of a Computer Based Examination followed by a skill test in stenography and document verification.  Qualified candidates should keep their educational certificates, category certificate, identity proof and recent photographs ready for document verification, and should regularly check the official website for the schedule of the next stage. The final merit and appointment are subject to successful completion of all remaining stages.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This recruitment is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a pass in the 12th Standard (10+2) or equivalent examination from a recognized Board. Candidates who qualify the Computer Based Examination are shortlisted for the stenography skill test as per the category-wise cut off. The prescribed age limit is 18 to 30 years for Grade C and 18 to 27 years for Grade D. Candidates should note that meeting the eligibility conditions is mandatory and will be strictly verified before final selection.</p><h3>Important Note</h3><p>Candidates should rely solely on the official website https://ssc.gov.in for authentic result-related information and must beware of fraudulent agents or unofficial websites that claim to influence results. Any grievance regarding the result should be addressed to the Staff Selection Commission through the prescribed official channel within the timeframe specified in the result notice, after which representations are generally not entertained.</p>', 'Central Govt', 'SSC', 'Staff Selection Commission', 'result', '2026-06-12', '2026-12-05', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-15', NULL, '2026-12-05', '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 2006, '18 to 30 years for Grade C and 18 to 27 years for Grade D', 'a pass in the 12th Standard (10+2) or equivalent examination from a recognized Board', 'Candidates who qualify the Computer Based Examination are shortlisted for the stenography skill test as per the category-wise cut off.', 100.00, 100.00, 0.00, 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in/stenographer-2026-result.pdf', 'https://ssc.gov.in/result', NULL, NULL, 'result', 'RESULT', 0, 1, 'SSC Stenographer 2026 Result – Check Skill Test Shortlist', 'SSC Stenographer 2026 CBE result declared. Check marks, category-wise cut off and skill test shortlist at ssc.gov.in using login credentials.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'IBPS RRB Office Assistant 2026 Prelims Result', 'ibps-rrb-office-assistant-2026-prelims-result', 'Institute of Banking Personnel Selection has declared the IBPS RRB Office Assistant 2026 preliminary result. Candidates can check their qualifying status at ibps.in to proceed to the main examination.', '<h2>IBPS RRB Office Assistant 2026 Prelims Result</h2><p>The Institute of Banking Personnel Selection has declared the <strong>result</strong> of the IBPS RRB Office Assistant 2026 Prelims Result examination on its official website https://ibps.in. Candidates who appeared in the examination can now check their qualifying status, marks and the category-wise cut off by logging in to the candidate portal or by checking the list of selected roll numbers published in the result notice. This result determines the candidates who are eligible to proceed to the next stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>About the Recruitment</h3><p>This recruitment is conducted by the Institute of Banking Personnel Selection for the post of IBPS RRB Office Assistant 2026 Prelims Result. Office Assistants handle clerical functions in Regional Rural Banks. The result is processed on the basis of the marks obtained by the candidates, after applying normalisation where the examination is held in multiple shifts, and the category-wise cut off marks determined by the conducting authority based on the number of vacancies, the number of candidates and the overall difficulty of the examination.</p><h3>How to Check the Result</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://ibps.in.</li><li>Click on the result link for the IBPS RRB Office Assistant 2026 Prelims Result examination.</li><li>A PDF containing the roll numbers of qualified or selected candidates will open.</li><li>Search for your roll number using the find option.</li><li>Log in with your registration number and date of birth to view your individual scorecard with detailed marks.</li></ol><h3>Cut Off Marks & Scorecard</h3><p>The cut off marks are released separately for each category, namely Unreserved, EWS, OBC, SC, ST and other applicable sub-categories. The individual scorecard displays the candidate''''s name, roll number, category, sectional and total marks, normalised marks where applicable, and the final qualifying status. Candidates are advised to download and preserve their scorecard, as it serves as an important record and may be required at later stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Next Steps for Qualified Candidates</h3><p>Candidates who have qualified must prepare for the subsequent stages of the selection process. The overall recruitment consists of a preliminary examination and a main examination, with the final merit based on the main examination.  Qualified candidates should keep their educational certificates, category certificate, identity proof and recent photographs ready for document verification, and should regularly check the official website for the schedule of the next stage. The final merit and appointment are subject to successful completion of all remaining stages.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This recruitment is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a graduation degree in any discipline from a recognized University with local language proficiency. Candidates who qualify the preliminary examination as per the state-wise cut off are eligible to appear in the single online main examination. The prescribed age limit is 18 to 28 years as on the cut-off date. Candidates should note that meeting the eligibility conditions is mandatory and will be strictly verified before final selection.</p><h3>Important Note</h3><p>Candidates should rely solely on the official website https://ibps.in for authentic result-related information and must beware of fraudulent agents or unofficial websites that claim to influence results. Any grievance regarding the result should be addressed to the Institute of Banking Personnel Selection through the prescribed official channel within the timeframe specified in the result notice, after which representations are generally not entertained.</p>', 'Bank', 'IBPS', 'Institute of Banking Personnel Selection', 'result', '2026-06-06', '2026-09-05', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-09', NULL, '2026-09-05', '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 9923, '18 to 28 years as on the cut-off date', 'a graduation degree in any discipline from a recognized University with local language proficiency', 'Candidates who qualify the preliminary examination as per the state-wise cut off are eligible to appear in the single online main examination.', 850.00, 850.00, 175.00, 'https://ibps.in', 'https://ibps.in', 'https://ibps.in/rrb-oa-2026-prelims-result.pdf', 'https://ibps.in/result', NULL, NULL, 'result', 'RESULT', 0, 1, 'IBPS RRB Office Assistant 2026 Prelims Result – Check at ibps.in', 'IBPS RRB Office Assistant 2026 preliminary result declared. Check qualifying status and cut off at ibps.in for the main examination.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'UPSC CDS (I) 2026 Result – Check Written Exam Result', 'upsc-cds-i-2026-result', 'UPSC has declared the Combined Defence Services Examination (I) 2026 written result. Candidates can check the list of qualified roll numbers at upsc.gov.in for the SSB interview.', '<h2>UPSC CDS (I) 2026 Result – Check Written Exam Result</h2><p>The Union Public Service Commission has declared the <strong>result</strong> of the UPSC CDS (I) 2026 Result examination on its official website https://upsc.gov.in. Candidates who appeared in the examination can now check their qualifying status, marks and the category-wise cut off by logging in to the candidate portal or by checking the list of selected roll numbers published in the result notice. This result determines the candidates who are eligible to proceed to the next stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>About the Recruitment</h3><p>This recruitment is conducted by the Union Public Service Commission for the post of UPSC CDS (I) 2026 Result. The CDS examination selects candidates for officer training in the defence academies. The result is processed on the basis of the marks obtained by the candidates, after applying normalisation where the examination is held in multiple shifts, and the category-wise cut off marks determined by the conducting authority based on the number of vacancies, the number of candidates and the overall difficulty of the examination.</p><h3>How to Check the Result</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://upsc.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the result link for the UPSC CDS (I) 2026 Result examination.</li><li>A PDF containing the roll numbers of qualified or selected candidates will open.</li><li>Search for your roll number using the find option.</li><li>Log in with your registration number and date of birth to view your individual scorecard with detailed marks.</li></ol><h3>Cut Off Marks & Scorecard</h3><p>The cut off marks are released separately for each category, namely Unreserved, EWS, OBC, SC, ST and other applicable sub-categories. The individual scorecard displays the candidate''''s name, roll number, category, sectional and total marks, normalised marks where applicable, and the final qualifying status. Candidates are advised to download and preserve their scorecard, as it serves as an important record and may be required at later stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Next Steps for Qualified Candidates</h3><p>Candidates who have qualified must prepare for the subsequent stages of the selection process. The overall recruitment consists of a written examination by UPSC, an SSB interview and a medical examination.  Qualified candidates should keep their educational certificates, category certificate, identity proof and recent photographs ready for document verification, and should regularly check the official website for the schedule of the next stage. The final merit and appointment are subject to successful completion of all remaining stages.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This recruitment is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline for IMA and OTA, and a degree with Physics and Mathematics or an Engineering degree for the Naval and Air Force academies. Candidates who qualify the written examination are called for the SSB interview and personality test. The prescribed age limit is approximately 19 to 25 years depending on the academy. Candidates should note that meeting the eligibility conditions is mandatory and will be strictly verified before final selection.</p><h3>Important Note</h3><p>Candidates should rely solely on the official website https://upsc.gov.in for authentic result-related information and must beware of fraudulent agents or unofficial websites that claim to influence results. Any grievance regarding the result should be addressed to the Union Public Service Commission through the prescribed official channel within the timeframe specified in the result notice, after which representations are generally not entertained.</p>', 'Defence', 'UPSC', 'Union Public Service Commission', 'result', '2025-12-20', '2026-06-12', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-04-12', NULL, '2026-06-12', '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 457, 'approximately 19 to 25 years depending on the academy', 'a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline for IMA and OTA, and a degree with Physics and Mathematics or an Engineering degree for the Naval and Air Force academies', 'Candidates who qualify the written examination are called for the SSB interview and personality test.', 200.00, 200.00, 0.00, 'https://upsc.gov.in', 'https://upsc.gov.in', 'https://upsc.gov.in/CDS-I-2026-Result.pdf', 'https://upsc.gov.in/examinations/results', NULL, NULL, 'result', 'RESULT', 0, 1, 'UPSC CDS 1 2026 Result – Check Written Exam Result at upsc.gov.in', 'UPSC CDS (I) 2026 written result declared. Check qualified roll numbers at upsc.gov.in for the SSB interview. Exam held on 12 April 2026.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
