(NULL, 'LIC AAO 2026 Prelims Result – Check Qualifying Status', 'lic-aao-2026-prelims-result', 'Life Insurance Corporation of India has declared the LIC AAO 2026 preliminary result. Candidates can check their qualifying status at licindia.in to proceed to the main examination.', '<h2>LIC AAO 2026 Prelims Result – Check Qualifying Status</h2><p>The Life Insurance Corporation of India has declared the <strong>result</strong> of the LIC AAO 2026 Prelims Result examination on its official website https://licindia.in. Candidates who appeared in the examination can now check their qualifying status, marks and the category-wise cut off by logging in to the candidate portal or by checking the list of selected roll numbers published in the result notice. This result determines the candidates who are eligible to proceed to the next stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>About the Recruitment</h3><p>This recruitment is conducted by the Life Insurance Corporation of India for the post of LIC AAO 2026 Prelims Result. The Assistant Administrative Officer post offers a respected managerial career. The result is processed on the basis of the marks obtained by the candidates, after applying normalisation where the examination is held in multiple shifts, and the category-wise cut off marks determined by the conducting authority based on the number of vacancies, the number of candidates and the overall difficulty of the examination.</p><h3>How to Check the Result</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://licindia.in.</li><li>Click on the result link for the LIC AAO 2026 Prelims Result examination.</li><li>A PDF containing the roll numbers of qualified or selected candidates will open.</li><li>Search for your roll number using the find option.</li><li>Log in with your registration number and date of birth to view your individual scorecard with detailed marks.</li></ol><h3>Cut Off Marks & Scorecard</h3><p>The cut off marks are released separately for each category, namely Unreserved, EWS, OBC, SC, ST and other applicable sub-categories. The individual scorecard displays the candidate''''s name, roll number, category, sectional and total marks, normalised marks where applicable, and the final qualifying status. Candidates are advised to download and preserve their scorecard, as it serves as an important record and may be required at later stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Next Steps for Qualified Candidates</h3><p>Candidates who have qualified must prepare for the subsequent stages of the selection process. The overall recruitment consists of a preliminary examination, a main examination, an interview and a pre-recruitment medical examination.  Qualified candidates should keep their educational certificates, category certificate, identity proof and recent photographs ready for document verification, and should regularly check the official website for the schedule of the next stage. The final merit and appointment are subject to successful completion of all remaining stages.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This recruitment is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a Bachelor''''s or Master''''s Degree with at least 60% marks for the Generalist post, and the relevant professional qualification for specialist posts. Candidates who qualify the preliminary examination as per the cut off are eligible to appear in the main examination. The prescribed age limit is 21 to 30 years as on the cut-off date. Candidates should note that meeting the eligibility conditions is mandatory and will be strictly verified before final selection.</p><h3>Important Note</h3><p>Candidates should rely solely on the official website https://licindia.in for authentic result-related information and must beware of fraudulent agents or unofficial websites that claim to influence results. Any grievance regarding the result should be addressed to the Life Insurance Corporation of India through the prescribed official channel within the timeframe specified in the result notice, after which representations are generally not entertained.</p>', 'Insurance', 'LIC', 'Life Insurance Corporation of India', 'result', '2026-06-04', '2026-08-18', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-08-08', NULL, '2026-08-18', '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 300, '21 to 30 years as on the cut-off date', 'a Bachelor''''s or Master''''s Degree with at least 60% marks for the Generalist post, and the relevant professional qualification for specialist posts', 'Candidates who qualify the preliminary examination as per the cut off are eligible to appear in the main examination.', 700.00, 700.00, 85.00, 'https://licindia.in', 'https://licindia.in', 'https://licindia.in/aao-2026-prelims-result.pdf', 'https://licindia.in/careers', NULL, NULL, 'result', 'RESULT', 0, 1, 'LIC AAO 2026 Prelims Result – Check Status at licindia.in', 'LIC AAO 2026 preliminary result declared. Check qualifying status and cut off at licindia.in. Qualified candidates appear in the main examination.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'SSC MTS 2026 Answer Key – Download Response Sheet & Objection', 'ssc-mts-2026-answer-key', 'Staff Selection Commission has released the SSC MTS 2026 tentative answer key. Candidates can download the response sheet and raise objections online at ssc.gov.in within the prescribed window.', '<h2>SSC MTS 2026 Answer Key – Download Response Sheet & Objection</h2><p>The Staff Selection Commission has released the <strong>provisional answer key</strong> for the SSC MTS 2026 Answer Key examination on its official website https://ssc.gov.in, along with the question paper and the candidate''''s recorded responses. This facility allows every candidate who appeared in the examination to verify their marked answers against the answers considered correct by the conducting authority, to estimate their probable score, and to raise objections against any answer they believe to be incorrect before the final result is processed.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Staff Selection Commission for the post of SSC MTS 2026 Answer Key. SSC MTS recruits Multi Tasking Staff and Havaldars for central government offices. The release of the provisional answer key is a transparent step in the evaluation process, as the final result is prepared only after considering all valid objections raised by the candidates during the prescribed window. The answer key facility is available through the candidate login for a limited number of days, usually three to five days.</p><h3>How to Download the Answer Key</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://ssc.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the answer key or response sheet link for the SSC MTS 2026 Answer Key examination.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password.</li><li>View your question paper, your marked responses and the provisional answer key.</li><li>Download and save a copy for calculating your score and preparing objections if required.</li></ol><h3>How to Raise Objections</h3><p>Candidates who are not satisfied with any answer in the provisional answer key can raise objections online during the specified window. A prescribed fee is charged for each question or answer challenged, which is refunded if the objection is found valid after review by a committee of subject experts. Candidates must provide proper justification and authentic references in support of each objection. Objections submitted after the deadline or through any mode other than the official online portal are not entertained under any circumstances.</p><h3>Importance of Reviewing the Answer Key</h3><p>Reviewing the answer key is crucial because the final result is prepared on the basis of the final answer key, which is published after evaluating all the objections received. By comparing their recorded responses with the provisional key, candidates can estimate their score using the applicable marking scheme, including the negative marking provisions, and assess their chances of qualifying for the next stage. This also helps candidates plan ahead for the subsequent stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a pass in the 10th class (Matriculation) from a recognized Board. Candidates who appeared in the Computer Based Examination can review the answer key and raise objections at the prescribed fee per question. The prescribed age limit is 18 to 25 years, with 18 to 27 years for some posts. The overall selection process consists of a Computer Based Examination, and for Havaldar posts a Physical Efficiency Test and Physical Standard Test. </p><h3>After the Objection Window</h3><p>Once the objection window closes, the subject experts of the Staff Selection Commission examine all the objections submitted by the candidates and prepare the final answer key. The result is then declared on the basis of this final key. Candidates are advised to regularly check the official website https://ssc.gov.in for the final answer key, result and the schedule of the next stage of the recruitment.</p>', 'Central Govt', 'SSC', 'Staff Selection Commission', 'notification', '2026-06-28', '2026-06-29', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-25', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 8000, '18 to 25 years, with 18 to 27 years for some posts', 'a pass in the 10th class (Matriculation) from a recognized Board', 'Candidates who appeared in the Computer Based Examination can review the answer key and raise objections at the prescribed fee per question.', 100.00, 100.00, 100.00, 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in/mts-2026-answer-key.pdf', 'https://ssc.gov.in/answer-key', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ANSWER_KEY', 0, 1, 'SSC MTS 2026 Answer Key – Response Sheet & Objection at ssc.gov.in', 'SSC MTS 2026 answer key released. Download response sheet and raise objections at ssc.gov.in within the objection window. Check marking scheme.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'SSC GD Constable 2026 Answer Key – Download & Raise Objection', 'ssc-gd-constable-2026-answer-key', 'Staff Selection Commission has released the SSC GD Constable 2026 tentative answer key. Candidates can download the response sheet and submit objections online at ssc.gov.in.', '<h2>SSC GD Constable 2026 Answer Key – Download & Raise Objection</h2><p>The Staff Selection Commission has released the <strong>provisional answer key</strong> for the SSC GD Constable 2026 Answer Key examination on its official website https://ssc.gov.in, along with the question paper and the candidate''''s recorded responses. This facility allows every candidate who appeared in the examination to verify their marked answers against the answers considered correct by the conducting authority, to estimate their probable score, and to raise objections against any answer they believe to be incorrect before the final result is processed.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Staff Selection Commission for the post of SSC GD Constable 2026 Answer Key. SSC GD Constable recruits for the Central Armed Police Forces and allied organisations. The release of the provisional answer key is a transparent step in the evaluation process, as the final result is prepared only after considering all valid objections raised by the candidates during the prescribed window. The answer key facility is available through the candidate login for a limited number of days, usually three to five days.</p><h3>How to Download the Answer Key</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://ssc.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the answer key or response sheet link for the SSC GD Constable 2026 Answer Key examination.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password.</li><li>View your question paper, your marked responses and the provisional answer key.</li><li>Download and save a copy for calculating your score and preparing objections if required.</li></ol><h3>How to Raise Objections</h3><p>Candidates who are not satisfied with any answer in the provisional answer key can raise objections online during the specified window. A prescribed fee is charged for each question or answer challenged, which is refunded if the objection is found valid after review by a committee of subject experts. Candidates must provide proper justification and authentic references in support of each objection. Objections submitted after the deadline or through any mode other than the official online portal are not entertained under any circumstances.</p><h3>Importance of Reviewing the Answer Key</h3><p>Reviewing the answer key is crucial because the final result is prepared on the basis of the final answer key, which is published after evaluating all the objections received. By comparing their recorded responses with the provisional key, candidates can estimate their score using the applicable marking scheme, including the negative marking provisions, and assess their chances of qualifying for the next stage. This also helps candidates plan ahead for the subsequent stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a pass in the 10th class (Matriculation) from a recognized Board. Candidates who appeared in the Computer Based Examination can review the answer key and raise objections at the prescribed fee per question. The prescribed age limit is 18 to 23 years as on the cut-off date. The overall selection process consists of a Computer Based Examination, a Physical Efficiency Test, a Physical Standard Test and a Detailed Medical Examination. </p><h3>After the Objection Window</h3><p>Once the objection window closes, the subject experts of the Staff Selection Commission examine all the objections submitted by the candidates and prepare the final answer key. The result is then declared on the basis of this final key. Candidates are advised to regularly check the official website https://ssc.gov.in for the final answer key, result and the schedule of the next stage of the recruitment.</p>', 'Central Govt', 'SSC', 'Staff Selection Commission', 'notification', '2026-02-20', '2026-02-21', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-15', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 39481, '18 to 23 years as on the cut-off date', 'a pass in the 10th class (Matriculation) from a recognized Board', 'Candidates who appeared in the Computer Based Examination can review the answer key and raise objections at the prescribed fee per question.', 100.00, 100.00, 100.00, 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in/gd-constable-2026-answer-key.pdf', 'https://ssc.gov.in/answer-key', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ANSWER_KEY', 0, 1, 'SSC GD Constable 2026 Answer Key – Objection Link at ssc.gov.in', 'SSC GD Constable 2026 answer key released. Download response sheet and raise objections at ssc.gov.in within the objection window.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'SSC JE 2026 Paper-I Answer Key – Download Response Sheet', 'ssc-je-2026-paper-1-answer-key', 'Staff Selection Commission has released the SSC JE 2026 Paper-I tentative answer key. Candidates can download the response sheet and raise objections online at ssc.gov.in.', '<h2>SSC JE 2026 Paper-I Answer Key – Download Response Sheet</h2><p>The Staff Selection Commission has released the <strong>provisional answer key</strong> for the SSC JE 2026 Paper-I Answer Key examination on its official website https://ssc.gov.in, along with the question paper and the candidate''''s recorded responses. This facility allows every candidate who appeared in the examination to verify their marked answers against the answers considered correct by the conducting authority, to estimate their probable score, and to raise objections against any answer they believe to be incorrect before the final result is processed.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Staff Selection Commission for the post of SSC JE 2026 Paper-I Answer Key. SSC JE recruits Junior Engineers for central government departments. The release of the provisional answer key is a transparent step in the evaluation process, as the final result is prepared only after considering all valid objections raised by the candidates during the prescribed window. The answer key facility is available through the candidate login for a limited number of days, usually three to five days.</p><h3>How to Download the Answer Key</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://ssc.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the answer key or response sheet link for the SSC JE 2026 Paper-I Answer Key examination.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password.</li><li>View your question paper, your marked responses and the provisional answer key.</li><li>Download and save a copy for calculating your score and preparing objections if required.</li></ol><h3>How to Raise Objections</h3><p>Candidates who are not satisfied with any answer in the provisional answer key can raise objections online during the specified window. A prescribed fee is charged for each question or answer challenged, which is refunded if the objection is found valid after review by a committee of subject experts. Candidates must provide proper justification and authentic references in support of each objection. Objections submitted after the deadline or through any mode other than the official online portal are not entertained under any circumstances.</p><h3>Importance of Reviewing the Answer Key</h3><p>Reviewing the answer key is crucial because the final result is prepared on the basis of the final answer key, which is published after evaluating all the objections received. By comparing their recorded responses with the provisional key, candidates can estimate their score using the applicable marking scheme, including the negative marking provisions, and assess their chances of qualifying for the next stage. This also helps candidates plan ahead for the subsequent stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a Diploma or Degree in the relevant Engineering discipline from a recognized institution or University. Candidates who appeared in the Paper-I Computer Based Examination can review the answer key and raise objections at the prescribed fee per question. The prescribed age limit is up to 30 to 32 years depending on the post. The overall selection process consists of a Paper-I and Paper-II Computer Based Examination and document verification. </p><h3>After the Objection Window</h3><p>Once the objection window closes, the subject experts of the Staff Selection Commission examine all the objections submitted by the candidates and prepare the final answer key. The result is then declared on the basis of this final key. Candidates are advised to regularly check the official website https://ssc.gov.in for the final answer key, result and the schedule of the next stage of the recruitment.</p>', 'Central Govt', 'SSC', 'Staff Selection Commission', 'notification', '2026-10-18', '2026-10-19', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-12', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 1340, 'up to 30 to 32 years depending on the post', 'a Diploma or Degree in the relevant Engineering discipline from a recognized institution or University', 'Candidates who appeared in the Paper-I Computer Based Examination can review the answer key and raise objections at the prescribed fee per question.', 100.00, 100.00, 100.00, 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in/je-2026-answer-key.pdf', 'https://ssc.gov.in/answer-key', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ANSWER_KEY', 0, 1, 'SSC JE 2026 Paper-I Answer Key – Response Sheet at ssc.gov.in', 'SSC JE 2026 Paper-I answer key released. Download response sheet and raise objections at ssc.gov.in within the objection window.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
