er key, result and the schedule of the next stage of the recruitment.</p>', 'Central Govt', 'SSC', 'Staff Selection Commission', 'notification', '2026-10-18', '2026-10-19', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-15', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 2006, '18 to 30 years for Grade C and 18 to 27 years for Grade D', 'a pass in the 12th Standard (10+2) from a recognized Board', 'Candidates who appeared in the Computer Based Examination can review the answer key and raise objections at the prescribed fee per question.', 100.00, 100.00, 100.00, 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in/stenographer-2026-answer-key.pdf', 'https://ssc.gov.in/answer-key', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ANSWER_KEY', 0, 1, 'SSC Stenographer 2026 Answer Key – Objection at ssc.gov.in', 'SSC Stenographer 2026 answer key released. Download response sheet and raise objections at ssc.gov.in within the objection window.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'RRB Group D 2026 CBT Answer Key – Download & Raise Objection', 'rrb-group-d-2026-cbt-answer-key', 'Railway Recruitment Boards have released the RRB Group D 2026 CBT answer key, question paper and response sheet. Candidates can raise objections online at rrbcdg.gov.in by paying the prescribed fee per question.', '<h2>RRB Group D 2026 CBT Answer Key – Download & Raise Objection</h2><p>The Railway Recruitment Boards has released the <strong>provisional answer key</strong> for the RRB Group D 2026 CBT Answer Key examination on its official website https://rrbcdg.gov.in, along with the question paper and the candidate''''s recorded responses. This facility allows every candidate who appeared in the examination to verify their marked answers against the answers considered correct by the conducting authority, to estimate their probable score, and to raise objections against any answer they believe to be incorrect before the final result is processed.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Railway Recruitment Boards for the post of RRB Group D 2026 CBT Answer Key. Group D posts form the operational backbone of Indian Railways. The release of the provisional answer key is a transparent step in the evaluation process, as the final result is prepared only after considering all valid objections raised by the candidates during the prescribed window. The answer key facility is available through the candidate login for a limited number of days, usually three to five days.</p><h3>How to Download the Answer Key</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://rrbcdg.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the answer key or response sheet link for the RRB Group D 2026 CBT Answer Key examination.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password.</li><li>View your question paper, your marked responses and the provisional answer key.</li><li>Download and save a copy for calculating your score and preparing objections if required.</li></ol><h3>How to Raise Objections</h3><p>Candidates who are not satisfied with any answer in the provisional answer key can raise objections online during the specified window. A prescribed fee is charged for each question or answer challenged, which is refunded if the objection is found valid after review by a committee of subject experts. Candidates must provide proper justification and authentic references in support of each objection. Objections submitted after the deadline or through any mode other than the official online portal are not entertained under any circumstances.</p><h3>Importance of Reviewing the Answer Key</h3><p>Reviewing the answer key is crucial because the final result is prepared on the basis of the final answer key, which is published after evaluating all the objections received. By comparing their recorded responses with the provisional key, candidates can estimate their score using the applicable marking scheme, including the negative marking provisions, and assess their chances of qualifying for the next stage. This also helps candidates plan ahead for the subsequent stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a 10th class pass, or a National Apprenticeship Certificate, or an ITI certificate from a recognized institution. Candidates who appeared in the Computer Based Test can review the answer key and raise objections at Rs. 50 per question, refundable if valid. The prescribed age limit is 18 to 36 years as on the cut-off date. The overall selection process consists of a single Computer Based Test, a Physical Efficiency Test, document verification and a medical examination. </p><h3>After the Objection Window</h3><p>Once the objection window closes, the subject experts of the Railway Recruitment Boards examine all the objections submitted by the candidates and prepare the final answer key. The result is then declared on the basis of this final key.