(NULL, 'UP Police Constable 2026 Answer Key – Download & Objection', 'up-police-constable-2026-answer-key', 'Uttar Pradesh Police Recruitment and Promotion Board has released the UP Police Constable 2026 answer key. Candidates can download the response sheet and submit objections online at uppbpb.gov.in.', '<h2>UP Police Constable 2026 Answer Key – Download & Objection</h2><p>The Uttar Pradesh Police Recruitment and Promotion Board has released the <strong>provisional answer key</strong> for the UP Police Constable 2026 Answer Key examination on its official website https://uppbpb.gov.in, along with the question paper and the candidate''''s recorded responses. This facility allows every candidate who appeared in the examination to verify their marked answers against the answers considered correct by the conducting authority, to estimate their probable score, and to raise objections against any answer they believe to be incorrect before the final result is processed.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Uttar Pradesh Police Recruitment and Promotion Board for the post of UP Police Constable 2026 Answer Key. The Constable post offers a stable career in the Uttar Pradesh Police. The release of the provisional answer key is a transparent step in the evaluation process, as the final result is prepared only after considering all valid objections raised by the candidates during the prescribed window. The answer key facility is available through the candidate login for a limited number of days, usually three to five days.</p><h3>How to Download the Answer Key</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://uppbpb.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the answer key or response sheet link for the UP Police Constable 2026 Answer Key examination.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password.</li><li>View your question paper, your marked responses and the provisional answer key.</li><li>Download and save a copy for calculating your score and preparing objections if required.</li></ol><h3>How to Raise Objections</h3><p>Candidates who are not satisfied with any answer in the provisional answer key can raise objections online during the specified window. A prescribed fee is charged for each question or answer challenged, which is refunded if the objection is found valid after review by a committee of subject experts. Candidates must provide proper justification and authentic references in support of each objection. Objections submitted after the deadline or through any mode other than the official online portal are not entertained under any circumstances.</p><h3>Importance of Reviewing the Answer Key</h3><p>Reviewing the answer key is crucial because the final result is prepared on the basis of the final answer key, which is published after evaluating all the objections received. By comparing their recorded responses with the provisional key, candidates can estimate their score using the applicable marking scheme, including the negative marking provisions, and assess their chances of qualifying for the next stage. This also helps candidates plan ahead for the subsequent stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a pass in the Intermediate (12th) examination from a Board recognized by the Government of Uttar Pradesh. Candidates who appeared in the written examination can review the answer key and raise objections at the prescribed fee per question. The prescribed age limit is 18 to 22 years for male and 18 to 25 years for female candidates. The overall selection process consists of a written examination, document verification, a physical standard test and a physical efficiency test. </p><h3>After the Objection Window</h3><p>Once the objection window closes, the subject experts of the Uttar Pradesh Police Recruitment and Promotion Board examine all the objections submitted by the candidates and prepare the final answer key. The result is then declared on the basis of this final key. Candidates are advised to regularly check the official website https://uppbpb.gov.in for the final answer key, result and the schedule of the next stage of the recruitment.</p>', 'State Govt', 'UPPRPB', 'Uttar Pradesh Police Recruitment and Promotion Board', 'notification', '2026-10-18', '2026-10-19', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-15', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 19220, '18 to 22 years for male and 18 to 25 years for female candidates', 'a pass in the Intermediate (12th) examination from a Board recognized by the Government of Uttar Pradesh', 'Candidates who appeared in the written examination can review the answer key and raise objections at the prescribed fee per question.', 400.00, 400.00, 400.00, 'https://uppbpb.gov.in', 'https://uppbpb.gov.in', 'https://uppbpb.gov.in/constable-2026-answer-key.pdf', 'https://uppbpb.gov.in/answer-key', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ANSWER_KEY', 0, 1, 'UP Police Constable 2026 Answer Key – Objection at uppbpb.gov.in', 'UP Police Constable 2026 answer key released. Download response sheet and raise objections at uppbpb.gov.in within the objection window.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
