ownload and save a copy for calculating your score and preparing objections if required.</li></ol><h3>How to Raise Objections</h3><p>Candidates who are not satisfied with any answer in the provisional answer key can raise objections online during the specified window. A prescribed fee is charged for each question or answer challenged, which is refunded if the objection is found valid after review by a committee of subject experts. Candidates must provide proper justification and authentic references in support of each objection. Objections submitted after the deadline or through any mode other than the official online portal are not entertained under any circumstances.</p><h3>Importance of Reviewing the Answer Key</h3><p>Reviewing the answer key is crucial because the final result is prepared on the basis of the final answer key, which is published after evaluating all the objections received. By comparing their recorded responses with the provisional key, candidates can estimate their score using the applicable marking scheme, including the negative marking provisions, and assess their chances of qualifying for the next stage. This also helps candidates plan ahead for the subsequent stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline from a recognized University or an equivalent qualification. Candidates who appeared in the preliminary examination can review the model answer key and submit objections within the prescribed window. The prescribed age limit is 21 to 40 years as on the cut-off date. The overall selection process consists of a preliminary examination, a main examination and an interview. </p><h3>After the Objection Window</h3><p>Once the objection window closes, the subject experts of the Madhya Pradesh Public Service Commission examine all the objections submitted by the candidates and prepare the final answer key. The result is then declared on the basis of this final key. Candidates are advised to regularly check the official website https://mppsc.mp.gov.in for the final answer key, result and the schedule of the next stage of the recruitment.</p>', 'State Govt', 'MPPSC', 'Madhya Pradesh Public Service Commission', 'notification', '2026-06-24', '2026-06-25', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-21', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 158, '21 to 40 years as on the cut-off date', 'a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline from a recognized University or an equivalent qualification', 'Candidates who appeared in the preliminary examination can review the model answer key and submit objections within the prescribed window.', 250.00, 250.00, 250.00, 'https://mppsc.mp.gov.in', 'https://mppsc.mp.gov.in', 'https://mppsc.mp.gov.in/state-service-prelims-2026-answer-key.pdf', 'https://mppsc.mp.gov.in', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ANSWER_KEY', 0, 1, 'MPPSC State Service Prelims 2026 Answer Key – Objection Online', 'MPPSC State Service Preliminary 2026 model answer key released. Download and submit objections at mppsc.mp.gov.in within the window.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'HSSC CET 2026 Answer Key – Download & Raise Objection Online', 'hssc-cet-2026-answer-key', 'Haryana Staff Selection Commission has released the Common Eligibility Test (CET) 2026 answer key. Candidates can download the response sheet and submit objections online at hssc.gov.in.', '<h2>HSSC CET 2026 Answer Key – Download & Raise Objection Online</h2><p>The Haryana Staff Selection Commission has released the <strong>provisional answer key</strong> for the HSSC CET 2026 Answer Key examination on its official website https://hssc.gov.in, along with the question paper and the candidate''''s recorded responses. This facility allows every candidate who appeared in the examination to verify their marked answers against the answers considered correct by the conducting authority, to estimate their probable score, and to raise objections against any answer they believe to be incorrect before the final result is processed.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Haryana Staff Selection Commission for the post of HSSC CET 2026 Answer Key. The CET is a common screening test for Group C and D posts in Haryana. The release of the provisional answer key is a transparent step in the evaluation process, as the final result is prepared only after considering all valid objections raised by the candidates during the prescribed window. The answer key facility is available through the candidate login for a limited number of days, usually three to five days.</p><h3>How to Download the Answer Key</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://hssc.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the answer key or response sheet link for the HSSC CET 2026 Answer Key examination.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password.</li><li>View your question paper, your marked responses and the provisional answer key.</li><li>Download and save a copy for calculating your score and preparing objections if required.</li></ol><h3>How to Raise Objections</h3><p>Candidates who are not satisfied with any answer in the provisional answer key can raise objections online during the specified window. A prescribed fee is charged for each question or answer challenged, which is refunded if the objection is found valid after review by a committee of subject experts. Candidates must provide proper justification and authentic references in support of each objection. Objections submitted after the deadline or through any mode other than the official online portal are not entertained under any circumstances.</p><h3>Importance of Reviewing the Answer Key</h3><p>Reviewing the answer key is crucial because the final result is prepared on the basis of the final answer key, which is published after evaluating all the objections received. By comparing their recorded responses with the provisional key, candidates can estimate their score using the applicable marking scheme, including the negative marking provisions, and assess their chances of qualifying for the next stage. This also helps candidates plan ahead for the subsequent stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a pass in the 10th, 12th or graduation as applicable to the Group of posts, from a recognized Board or University. Candidates who appeared in the Common Eligibility Test can review the answer key and raise objections at the prescribed fee per question. The prescribed age limit is 18 to 42 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation as per Haryana government rules. The overall selection process consists of a Common Eligibility Test, followed by a post-specific examination and document verification. </p><h3>After the Objection Window</h3><p>Once the objection window closes, the subject experts of the Haryana Staff Selection Commission examine all the objections submitted by the candidates and prepare the final answer key. The result is then declared on the basis of this fina