(NULL, 'UPPSC PCS Prelims 2026 Answer Key – Download & Raise Objection', 'uppsc-pcs-prelims-2026-answer-key', 'Uttar Pradesh Public Service Commission has released the PCS Preliminary 2026 answer key. Candidates can download the answer key and submit objections online at uppsc.up.nic.in within the prescribed window.', '<h2>UPPSC PCS Prelims 2026 Answer Key – Download & Raise Objection</h2><p>The Uttar Pradesh Public Service Commission has released the <strong>provisional answer key</strong> for the UPPSC PCS Prelims 2026 Answer Key examination on its official website https://uppsc.up.nic.in, along with the question paper and the candidate''''s recorded responses. This facility allows every candidate who appeared in the examination to verify their marked answers against the answers considered correct by the conducting authority, to estimate their probable score, and to raise objections against any answer they believe to be incorrect before the final result is processed.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Uttar Pradesh Public Service Commission for the post of UPPSC PCS Prelims 2026 Answer Key. The PCS examination recruits for administrative and police service posts in Uttar Pradesh. The release of the provisional answer key is a transparent step in the evaluation process, as the final result is prepared only after considering all valid objections raised by the candidates during the prescribed window. The answer key facility is available through the candidate login for a limited number of days, usually three to five days.</p><h3>How to Download the Answer Key</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://uppsc.up.nic.in.</li><li>Click on the answer key or response sheet link for the UPPSC PCS Prelims 2026 Answer Key examination.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password.</li><li>View your question paper, your marked responses and the provisional answer key.</li><li>Download and save a copy for calculating your score and preparing objections if required.</li></ol><h3>How to Raise Objections</h3><p>Candidates who are not satisfied with any answer in the provisional answer key can raise objections online during the specified window. A prescribed fee is charged for each question or answer challenged, which is refunded if the objection is found valid after review by a committee of subject experts. Candidates must provide proper justification and authentic references in support of each objection. Objections submitted after the deadline or through any mode other than the official online portal are not entertained under any circumstances.</p><h3>Importance of Reviewing the Answer Key</h3><p>Reviewing the answer key is crucial because the final result is prepared on the basis of the final answer key, which is published after evaluating all the objections received. By comparing their recorded responses with the provisional key, candidates can estimate their score using the applicable marking scheme, including the negative marking provisions, and assess their chances of qualifying for the next stage. This also helps candidates plan ahead for the subsequent stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline from a recognized University or an equivalent qualification. Candidates who appeared in the preliminary examination can review the answer key and submit objections at the prescribed fee per question. The prescribed age limit is 21 to 40 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation as per UP government rules. The overall selection process consists of a preliminary examination, a main examination and an interview. </p><h3>After the Objection Window</h3><p>Once the objection window closes, the subject experts of the Uttar Pradesh Public Service Commission examine all the objections submitted by the candidates and prepare the final answer key. The result is then declared on the basis of this final key. Candidates are advised to regularly check the official website https://uppsc.up.nic.in for the final answer key, result and the schedule of the next stage of the recruitment.</p>', 'State Govt', 'UPPSC', 'Uttar Pradesh Public Service Commission', 'notification', '2026-06-24', '2026-06-25', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-21', NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 220, '21 to 40 years as on the cut-off date, with relaxation as per UP government rules', 'a Bachelor''''s Degree in any discipline from a recognized University or an equivalent qualification', 'Candidates who appeared in the preliminary examination can review the answer key and submit objections at the prescribed fee per question.', 125.00, 125.00, 65.00, 'https://uppsc.up.nic.in', 'https://uppsc.up.nic.in', 'https://uppsc.up.nic.in/pcs-prelims-2026-answer-key.pdf', 'https://uppsc.up.nic.in/answer-key', NULL, NULL, 'active', 'ANSWER_KEY', 0, 1, 'UPPSC PCS Prelims 2026 Answer Key – Objection at uppsc.up.nic.in', 'UPPSC PCS Preliminary 2026 answer key released. Download and submit objections at uppsc.up.nic.in within the objection window.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'SSC Selection Post Phase XIV 2026 Admit Card – Download Online', 'ssc-selection-post-phase-xiv-2026-admit-card', 'Staff Selection Commission has released the SSC Selection Post Phase XIV 2026 admit card. Candidates can download their region-wise hall ticket from ssc.gov.in and the regional SSC websites using their login credentials.', '<h2>SSC Selection Post Phase XIV 2026 Admit Card – Download Online</h2><p>The Staff Selection Commission has released the <strong>admit card</strong> for the SSC Selection Post Phase XIV 2026 Admit Card examination on its official website https://ssc.gov.in. The admit card, also known as the call letter or hall ticket, is one of the most important documents that every candidate must carry to the examination centre, since no candidate is permitted to enter the examination hall without a valid printed admit card and a matching original photo identity proof. Candidates who successfully submitted their applications can now download their admit card by logging in with their credentials.</p><h3>About the Examination</h3><p>This examination is conducted by the Staff Selection Commission as part of the selection process for the post of SSC Selection Post Phase XIV 2026 Admit Card. The Selection Post examination fills a wide variety of posts across central government departments at different qualification levels. The admit card contains essential information such as the candidate''''s name, roll number, registration number, photograph, signature, examination date, reporting time, shift, and the complete address of the allotted examination centre, along with detailed instructions that every candidate must read and follow carefully on the day of the examination.</p><h3>How to Download the Admit Card</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://ssc.gov.in.</li><li>Click on the admit card or call letter download link for SSC Selection Post Phase XIV 2026 Admit Card.</li><li>Log in using your registration number, roll number, date of birth or password as applicable.</li><li>The admit card will be displayed on the screen with all your examination details.</li><li>Verify the details, download the admit card and take a clear printout on A4 size paper.</li></ol><h3>Documents to Carry</h3><p>Candidates must carry the printed copy of the admit card along with at least one original valid photo identity proof such as Aadhaar Card, Voter ID, PAN Card, Driving Licence or Passport. A recent passport-size colour photograph identical to the one uploaded during the application must also be carried and affixed where required. Candidates who fail to bring these documents will not be allowed to appear in the examination under any circumstances.</p><h3>Important Instructions</h3><p>Candidates are advised to reach the examination centre well before the reporting time indicated on the admit card, as late entry is strictly prohibited. Biometric verification, frisking and document checks are carried out at the centre and may take considerable time. Electronic gadgets including mobile phones, calculators, smartwatches, Bluetooth devices, and any printed or written study material are strictly banned inside the examination hall. Candidates must carefully verify every detail printed on the admit card and immediately report any discrepancy to the conducting authority.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This examination is open to candidates who meet the prescribed qualification, namely a pass in the 10th, 12th or graduation as applicable to the specific post category (Matriculation, Higher Secondary or Graduation level), from a recognized Board or University. Candidates whose applications were accepted for the relevant post level can download the admit card for the Computer Based Examination from the respective regional website. The age criterion for the post is 18 to 30 years depending on the post and the recruiting department. Candidates appearing in the examination should ensure that they continue to satisfy all eligibility conditions, as these are verified during the document verification stage that follows the written examination.</p><h3>Selection Process & Next Steps</h3><p>The overall selection for this recruitment consists of a Computer Based Examination followed by document verification and a skill test where applicable.  After appearing in the examination for which this admit card is issued, candidates should regularly monitor the official website https://ssc.gov.in for the answer key, result and the schedule of subsequent stages. It is advisable to retain the admit card safely even after the examination, as it is often required at later stages such as document verification and counselling.</p>', 'Central Govt', 'SSC', 'Staff Selection Commission', 'admitcard', '2026-04-25', '2026-06-12', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-22', '2026-06-12', NULL, '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 2423, '18 to 30 years depending on the post and the recruiting department', 'a pass in the 10th, 12th or graduation as applicable to the specific post category (Matriculation, Higher Secondary or Graduation level), from a recognized Board or University', 'Candidates whose applications were accepted for the relevant post level can download the admit card for the Computer Based Examination from the respective regional website.', 100.00, 100.00, 0.00, 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in', 'https://ssc.gov.in/selection-post-xiv-2026-admit.pdf', 'https://ssc.gov.in/admit-card', NULL, NULL, 'admitcard', 'ADMIT_CARD', 0, 1, 'SSC Selection Post Phase XIV 2026 Admit Card – Download Online', 'SSC Selection Post Phase XIV 2026 admit card released. Download region-wise hall ticket at ssc.gov.in using login credentials. Check exam pattern.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP),
(NULL, 'AFCAT 01/2026 Result – Check Air Force Written Exam Result', 'afcat-01-2026-result', 'Indian Air Force has declared the AFCAT 01/2026 written examination result. Candidates can check their qualifying status at afcat.cdac.in to proceed to the Air Force Selection Board testing.', '<h2>AFCAT 01/2026 Result – Check Air Force Written Exam Result</h2><p>The Indian Air Force has declared the <strong>result</strong> of the AFCAT 01/2026 Result examination on its official website https://afcat.cdac.in. Candidates who appeared in the examination can now check their qualifying status, marks and the category-wise cut off by logging in to the candidate portal or by checking the list of selected roll numbers published in the result notice. This result determines the candidates who are eligible to proceed to the next stage of the recruitment process.</p><h3>About the Recruitment</h3><p>This recruitment is conducted by the Indian Air Force for the post of AFCAT 01/2026 Result. AFCAT is the entry test for a commissioned officer career in the Indian Air Force. The result is processed on the basis of the marks obtained by the candidates, after applying normalisation where the examination is held in multiple shifts, and the category-wise cut off marks determined by the conducting authority based on the number of vacancies, the number of candidates and the overall difficulty of the examination.</p><h3>How to Check the Result</h3><ol><li>Visit the official website https://afcat.cdac.in.</li><li>Click on the result link for the AFCAT 01/2026 Result examination.</li><li>A PDF containing the roll numbers of qualified or selected candidates will open.</li><li>Search for your roll number using the find option.</li><li>Log in with your registration number and date of birth to view your individual scorecard with detailed marks.</li></ol><h3>Cut Off Marks & Scorecard</h3><p>The cut off marks are released separately for each category, namely Unreserved, EWS, OBC, SC, ST and other applicable sub-categories. The individual scorecard displays the candidate''''s name, roll number, category, sectional and total marks, normalised marks where applicable, and the final qualifying status. Candidates are advised to download and preserve their scorecard, as it serves as an important record and may be required at later stages of the recruitment.</p><h3>Next Steps for Qualified Candidates</h3><p>Candidates who have qualified must prepare for the subsequent stages of the selection process. The overall recruitment consists of the online AFCAT examination, Air Force Selection Board testing and a medical examination.  Qualified candidates should keep their educational certificates, category certificate, identity proof and recent photographs ready for document verification, and should regularly check the official website for the schedule of the next stage. The final merit and appointment are subject to successful completion of all remaining stages.</p><h3>Eligibility Recap</h3><p>This recruitment is open to candidates fulfilling the qualification of a graduation degree with the prescribed marks for the Flying Branch, and the relevant engineering or graduation/post-graduation degree for the Technical and Ground Duty branches. Candidates who qualify the AFCAT written examination as per the cut off are called for the Air Force Selection Board testing and interview. The prescribed age limit is 20 to 24 years for the Flying Branch and 20 to 26 years for the Ground Duty branches. Candidates should note that meeting the eligibility conditions is mandatory and will be strictly verified before final selection.</p><h3>Important Note</h3><p>Candidates should rely solely on the official website https://afcat.cdac.in for authentic result-related information and must beware of fraudulent agents or unofficial websites that claim to influence results. Any grievance regarding the result should be addressed to the Indian Air Force through the prescribed official channel within the timeframe specified in the result notice, after which representations are generally not entertained.</p>', 'Defence', 'Indian Air Force', 'Indian Air Force', 'result', '2025-12-01', '2026-06-10', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-02-22', NULL, '2026-06-10', '2026-06-19 10:00:00', 304, '20 to 24 years for the Flying Branch and 20 to 26 years for the Ground Duty branches', 'a graduation degree with the prescribed marks for the Flying Branch, and the relevant engineering or graduation/post-graduation degree for the Technical and Ground Duty branches', 'Candidates who qualify the AFCAT written examination as per the cut off are called for the Air Force Selection Board testing and interview.', 550.00, 550.00, 550.00, 'https://afcat.cdac.in', 'https://afcat.cdac.in', 'https://afcat.cdac.in/afcat-01-2026-result.pdf', 'https://afcat.cdac.in', NULL, NULL, 'result', 'RESULT', 0, 1, 'AFCAT 01/2026 Result – Check Written Exam Result at afcat.cdac.in', 'AFCAT 01/2026 written exam result declared. Check qualifying status at afcat.cdac.in for the Air Force Selection Board testing.', NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
